const MOCK_BANK={"listen":[{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"👔 📋 ☕ 🏢","audio":"A man is giving a presentation to his colleagues.","q":"What is the man doing?","o":["Drinking coffee","Waiting for a bus","Giving a presentation","Filing reports"],"a":2,"zh":"一位男士正在向同事做簡報。","kw":["giving a presentation","colleagues"],"why":"問題問男士在做什麼，音檔原話 giving a presentation 直接對應選項 C，其餘選項音檔都沒提到。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"👩‍💻 💻 🖨️ 📊","audio":"A woman is typing on a computer keyboard.","q":"What is the woman doing?","o":["Printing a document","Typing on a keyboard","Answering the phone","Filing paperwork"],"a":1,"zh":"一位女士正在電腦鍵盤上打字。","kw":["typing","computer keyboard"],"why":"音檔說 typing on a computer keyboard，對應選項 B。列印、接電話、歸檔都是圖中沒有的動作。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"📞 😊 👩 📋","audio":"A receptionist is answering a telephone call.","q":"What is the receptionist doing?","o":["Writing a report","Meeting a client","Serving food","Answering a telephone"],"a":3,"zh":"一位接待員正在接聽電話。","kw":["answering","telephone"],"why":"音檔原話 answering a telephone call 直接對應選項 D。其餘選項的動作在圖中與音檔中皆未出現。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"🚗 🔧 ⛽ 🅿️","audio":"A mechanic is repairing a car engine.","q":"What is the mechanic doing?","o":["Repairing a car engine","Washing a car","Driving a truck","Parking a car"],"a":0,"zh":"一位技工正在修理汽車引擎。","kw":["repairing","car engine"],"why":"repairing a car engine 與「修理汽車引擎」完全一致，選項 A 正確。洗車、開卡車、停車都是看似相關的干擾動作。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"🛒 🥦 🧀 💰","audio":"A customer is paying for groceries at the checkout counter.","q":"What is the customer doing?","o":["Choosing vegetables","Returning an item","Paying for groceries","Stocking shelves"],"a":2,"zh":"一位顧客正在結帳櫃台付帳購買雜貨。","kw":["paying for groceries","checkout counter"],"why":"音檔說在 checkout counter 付帳買雜貨，對應選項 C。挑選蔬菜、退貨、補貨都不是圖中的動作。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"🍽️ 👨‍🍳 🥗 🔪","audio":"A chef is chopping vegetables on a cutting board.","q":"What is the chef doing?","o":["Cooking a steak","Chopping vegetables","Washing dishes","Setting the table"],"a":1,"zh":"一位廚師正在砧板上切蔬菜。","kw":["chopping vegetables","cutting board"],"why":"chopping vegetables 就是切蔬菜，與選項 B 完全相符。煎牛排、洗碗、擺餐桌都沒有證據。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"✈️ 🧳 🗓️ 🛂","audio":"A traveler is checking in at the airport counter.","q":"What is the traveler doing?","o":["Boarding a plane","Buying a souvenir","Claiming luggage","Checking in at the airport"],"a":3,"zh":"一位旅客正在機場櫃台辦理報到手續。","kw":["checking in","airport"],"why":"checking in at the airport 指在機場櫃台報到，對應選項 D。登機、買紀念品、領行李是不同階段的動作。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"👩‍💼 📊 📈 🗣️","audio":"A woman is pointing at a chart during a meeting.","q":"What is the woman doing?","o":["Pointing at a chart","Taking notes","Serving coffee","Opening a window"],"a":0,"zh":"一位女士在會議中指著圖表。","kw":["pointing","chart"],"why":"音檔的 pointing at a chart 直接對應選項 A「指著圖表」。記筆記、倒咖啡、開窗戶皆未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"🎾 🤝 🏟️ 🎾","audio":"Two players are shaking hands after a tennis match.","q":"What are the players doing?","o":["Serving the ball","Buying tickets","Shaking hands","Cheering loudly"],"a":2,"zh":"兩位選手在網球比賽後握手。","kw":["shaking hands","tennis match"],"why":"音檔說賽後 shaking hands，只有選項 C 描述此動作。發球、買票、歡呼都與音檔不符。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"📚 🤫 🧑‍🏫 🪑","audio":"A librarian is shelving books in the library.","q":"What is the librarian doing?","o":["Reading a newspaper","Shelving books","Returning a book","Borrowing a CD"],"a":1,"zh":"一位圖書館員正在圖書館上架書籍。","kw":["shelving books","library"],"why":"shelving books 即把書放上書架，對應選項 B。讀報紙、還書、借 CD 都是讀者可能做的動作，不是圖書館員正在做的事。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"🧺 👗 🌧️ 🧵","audio":"A woman is hanging laundry on a clothesline.","q":"What is the woman doing?","o":["Ironing a shirt","Folding towels","Buying clothes","Hanging laundry"],"a":3,"zh":"一位女士正在晾衣繩上曬衣服。","kw":["hanging laundry","clothesline"],"why":"hanging laundry on a clothesline 就是在晾衣繩曬衣服，對應選項 D。熨衫、折毛巾、買衣服都與音檔不同。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"🐕 🦮 🌳 🚶","audio":"A man is walking his dog in the park.","q":"What is the man doing?","o":["Walking his dog","Riding a bicycle","Feeding a cat","Driving a car"],"a":0,"zh":"一位男士正在公園遛狗。","kw":["walking his dog","park"],"why":"音檔原話 walking his dog 對應選項 A。騎腳踏車、餵貓、開車都沒有出現在音檔中。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"🎂 🕯️ 🎈 🎉","audio":"The children are blowing out the candles on a birthday cake.","q":"What are the children doing?","o":["Cutting the cake","Opening presents","Blowing out candles","Singing a song"],"a":2,"zh":"孩子們正在吹熄生日蛋糕上的蠟燭。","kw":["blowing out","birthday cake"],"why":"blowing out the candles 就是吹熄蠟燭，選項 C 為唯一正確答案。切蛋糕、拆禮物、唱歌雖是生日場景，但音檔未提。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"☕ 💬 🪑 👫","audio":"Two colleagues are chatting over coffee in the cafeteria.","q":"What are the colleagues doing?","o":["Having a job interview","Chatting over coffee","Reading the newspaper","Eating alone"],"a":1,"zh":"兩位同事正在自助餐廳邊喝咖啡聊天。","kw":["chatting over coffee","cafeteria"],"why":"chatting over coffee 指邊喝咖啡聊天，直接對應選項 B。面試、看報紙、獨自吃飯都不符合音檔描述。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"🧳 ✈️ 🌍 📍","audio":"A family is boarding a plane for their vacation.","q":"What is the family doing?","o":["Packing their bags","Waiting at the gate","Renting a car","Boarding a plane"],"a":3,"zh":"一家人正在登機準備去度假。","kw":["boarding a plane","vacation"],"why":"boarding a plane 是登機，與選項 D 完全一致。打包、在閘口等候、租車都是不同階段的動作。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"🧴 😷 🩺 💉","audio":"A nurse is giving a patient an injection in the arm.","q":"What is the nurse doing?","o":["Giving an injection","Checking blood pressure","Writing a prescription","Measuring temperature"],"a":0,"zh":"一位護士正在為病人的手臂打針。","kw":["giving","injection"],"why":"giving an injection 就是施打針劑，對應選項 A。量血壓、開處方、量體溫都是醫療動作但非音檔所述。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"🖥️ 📞 👨‍💼 🗂️","audio":"A man is typing an email at his desk.","q":"What is the man doing?","o":["Talking on the phone","Filing documents","Typing an email","Drinking tea"],"a":2,"zh":"一位男士正在桌前撰寫電子郵件。","kw":["typing","email"],"why":"音檔 typing an email 對應選項 C「撰寫電子郵件」。接電話、歸檔文件、喝茶都未出現在音檔。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"🎓 🎓 🎉 👨‍🎓","audio":"The students are throwing their graduation caps into the air.","q":"What are the students doing?","o":["Attending a lecture","Throwing their caps","Taking a final exam","Studying in the library"],"a":1,"zh":"學生們正把畢業帽拋向空中。","kw":["throwing","graduation caps"],"why":"throwing their graduation caps 就是拋畢業帽，對應選項 B。上課、期末考、圖書館自習都與音檔情境不符。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"🐕 🕳️ 🦴 🐾","audio":"A dog is digging a hole in the backyard.","q":"What is the dog doing?","o":["Chasing a ball","Sleeping on the rug","Eating from a bowl","Digging a hole"],"a":3,"zh":"一隻狗正在後院挖洞。","kw":["digging","hole"],"why":"digging a hole 是挖洞，與選項 D 一致。追球、睡覺、吃東西都是狗常見動作，但音檔沒提。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"🌧️ ☂️ 🏃 🚌","audio":"A woman is running to catch a bus in the rain.","q":"What is the woman doing?","o":["Running to catch a bus","Driving a car","Waiting at a bus stop","Hailing a taxi"],"a":0,"zh":"一位女士正在雨中奔跑趕公車。","kw":["running","bus"],"why":"音檔說 running to catch a bus，選項 A 完全符合。開車、在站牌等車、攔計程車都不是她正在做的動作。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"🧗 🪨 🏔️ 🧗‍♀️","audio":"A man is climbing up a rocky mountain.","q":"What is the man doing?","o":["Skiing down a hill","Camping in a forest","Climbing up a mountain","Fishing by the lake"],"a":2,"zh":"一位男士正在攀爬岩石山。","kw":["climbing","mountain"],"why":"climbing up a rocky mountain 即攀爬岩山，對應選項 C。滑雪、露營、釣魚都與音檔動作不同。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"🎹 🎵 👩‍🎤 🎤","audio":"A woman is playing the piano on stage.","q":"What is the woman doing?","o":["Singing into a microphone","Playing the piano","Tuning a guitar","Dancing with a partner"],"a":1,"zh":"一位女士正在舞台上彈鋼琴。","kw":["playing","piano"],"why":"playing the piano 就是彈鋼琴，選項 B 正確。唱歌、調吉他、跳舞皆未被音檔描述。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"🐟 🎣 🛶 🌅","audio":"A man is fishing from a small boat on the lake.","q":"What is the man doing?","o":["Swimming in the lake","Rowing to the shore","Water-skiing","Fishing from a boat"],"a":3,"zh":"一位男士正在湖上的小船釣魚。","kw":["fishing","boat"],"why":"fishing from a small boat 指在小船上釣魚，對應選項 D。游泳、划向岸邊、滑水都是湖上活動但非音檔所述。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"📦 🚚 🏃‍♂️ 📋","audio":"Delivery workers are unloading boxes from a truck.","q":"What are the workers doing?","o":["Unloading boxes from a truck","Loading furniture","Driving a forklift","Signing for a package"],"a":0,"zh":"送貨員正在從卡車上卸下箱子。","kw":["unloading","truck"],"why":"unloading boxes from a truck 就是從卡車卸貨，對應選項 A。裝家具、開堆高機、簽收包裹都不是音檔描述的動作。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"🖌️ 🎨 🖼️ 👩","audio":"An artist is painting a landscape on a canvas.","q":"What is the artist doing?","o":["Sketching a portrait","Hanging a picture","Painting a landscape","Mixing cement"],"a":2,"zh":"一位藝術家正在畫布上畫風景。","kw":["painting","landscape"],"why":"painting a landscape 指畫風景畫，對應選項 C。素描人像、掛畫、攪拌水泥都與音檔動作不符。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"🧊 ❄️ 🧣 🍂","audio":"A man is shivering because of the cold weather.","q":"What is the man doing?","o":["Sweating in the heat","Shivering from the cold","Opening a window","Wearing sunglasses"],"a":1,"zh":"因為天氣寒冷，一位男士正在發抖。","kw":["shivering","cold"],"why":"shivering because of the cold 就是冷得發抖，對應選項 B。流汗、開窗、戴太陽眼鏡都是炎熱天氣的動作。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"🪟 🧽 👩 🏠","audio":"A woman is cleaning the windows of her house.","q":"What is the woman doing?","o":["Painting the fence","Repairing the roof","Mowing the lawn","Cleaning the windows"],"a":3,"zh":"一位女士正在清洗房子的窗戶。","kw":["cleaning","windows"],"why":"cleaning the windows 就是擦窗戶，與選項 D 完全一致。漆籬笆、修屋頂、割草都是庭院工作但音檔沒提。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"🐕 🛁 🧼 🌳","audio":"A man is giving his dog a bath in the backyard.","q":"What is the man doing?","o":["Giving his dog a bath","Trimming the dog's nails","Playing fetch","Walking the dog"],"a":0,"zh":"一位男士正在後院幫狗洗澡。","kw":["giving","bath"],"why":"giving his dog a bath 是幫狗洗澡，選項 A 正確。剪指甲、玩接球、遛狗都是與狗有關的動作，但不是音檔所述。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"👩‍💼 📄 ✍️ 🖊️","audio":"A woman is signing a contract at her office desk.","q":"What is the woman doing?","o":["Reading a newspaper","Making a phone call","Signing a contract","Shredding documents"],"a":2,"zh":"一位女士正在辦公桌前簽署合約。","kw":["signing","contract"],"why":"signing a contract 即簽合約，直接對應選項 C。讀報、打電話、碎文件都是辦公室常見動作但音檔未提。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 1","emoji":"🏟️ ⚽ 🙌 👟","audio":"The soccer players are celebrating a goal on the field.","q":"What are the players doing?","o":["Blowing a whistle","Celebrating a goal","Buying tickets","Getting injured"],"a":1,"zh":"足球選手們正在球場上慶祝進球。","kw":["celebrating","goal"],"why":"celebrating a goal 是慶祝進球，選項 B 為唯一正確答案。吹哨、買票、受傷都與音檔描述不符。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"What time does the meeting start?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["In the conference room.","It starts at three.","With Mr. Smith.","About an hour."],"a":1,"zh":"會議幾點開始？→ 三點開始。","kw":["What time","meeting"],"why":"What time 問時間，只有選項 B 回答時間；A 回地點、C 回人物、D 回長度，皆答非所問。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"Where should I park my car?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["At ten o'clock.","About fifty dollars.","Mr. Lee is the manager.","In the parking lot behind the building."],"a":3,"zh":"我該把車停在哪裡？→ 停在大樓後面的停車場。","kw":["Where","park"],"why":"Where 問地點，選項 D 是地點回答。A 是時間、B 是金額、C 是人物，詞性相近但答非所問。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"Who is in charge of the marketing department?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["Ms. Chen is.","Since last April.","On the third floor.","By express mail."],"a":0,"zh":"誰負責行銷部門？→ 陳女士。","kw":["Who","marketing department"],"why":"Who 問人物，選項 A 回答人物。B 回時間、C 回地點、D 回方式，都是常見陷阱。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"How much does the train ticket cost?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["For two people.","At the ticket office.","Twenty-five dollars.","Tomorrow morning."],"a":2,"zh":"火車票多少錢？→ 二十五美元。","kw":["How much","ticket"],"why":"How much 問金額，選項 C 是金額。A 是數量、B 是地點、D 是時間，皆不對題。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"When was the report submitted?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["To the head office.","Yesterday afternoon.","By Mr. Brown.","In three copies."],"a":1,"zh":"報告是什麼時候提交的？→ 昨天下午。","kw":["When","report"],"why":"When 問時間，選項 B 回答時間。A 回地點、C 回人物、D 回份數，皆為答非所問。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"Why was the flight canceled?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["Because of the heavy snow.","At Gate 12.","For business class.","On Singapore Airlines."],"a":0,"zh":"航班為何取消？→ 因為大雪。","kw":["Why","flight"],"why":"Why 問原因，選項 A 的 Because 直接回答原因。B 回登機門、C 回艙等、D 回航空公司，都是陷阱。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"How do I get to the convention center?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["About twenty minutes.","Twenty dollars per person.","Ms. Wilson did.","Take the number 7 bus."],"a":3,"zh":"我要怎麼到會展中心？→ 搭 7 號公車。","kw":["How","convention center"],"why":"How 問方式，選項 D 給搭乘方式。A 回時間長短、B 回金額、C 回人物，皆不符合問法。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"Which floor is the human resources office on?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["At nine sharp.","It's on the fifth floor.","Mr. Gonzalez.","By registered mail."],"a":1,"zh":"人力資源辦公室在幾樓？→ 在五樓。","kw":["Which floor","human resources"],"why":"Which floor 問樓層，選項 B 回答樓層。A 回時間、C 回人物、D 回寄送方式，皆答非所問。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"What is the main topic of tomorrow's seminar?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["Customer satisfaction strategies.","In the main hall.","Dr. Lopez will speak.","Registration is free."],"a":0,"zh":"明天研討會的主題是什麼？→ 顧客滿意策略。","kw":["main topic","seminar"],"why":"What 問主題內容，選項 A 是主題。B 回地點、C 回講者、D 回費用，皆為相關但不對題的資訊。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"Could you tell me when the store closes?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["The manager is on duty.","Across from the post office.","It closes at nine p.m.","It sells fresh bread."],"a":2,"zh":"請問這家店幾點打烊？→ 晚上九點。","kw":["when","closes"],"why":"when 問時間，選項 C 回答打烊時間。A 回人物、B 回地點、D 回販售商品，都是陷阱。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"Would you like some more coffee?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["It's on the second floor.","No, thank you. I'm fine.","About half an hour.","His name is Daniel."],"a":1,"zh":"你要再來點咖啡嗎？→ 不用了，謝謝。","kw":["Would you like","coffee"],"why":"Would you like 問意願，選項 B 是恰當的婉拒。A 回地點、C 回時間、D 回人物，完全不搭。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"Have you finished the inventory list?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["In the storage room.","Since last Monday.","She is the supervisor.","Not yet, but I'll send it soon."],"a":3,"zh":"你完成庫存清單了嗎？→ 還沒有，但很快會寄出。","kw":["inventory list","finished"],"why":"問是否完成，選項 D 直接回答進度。A 回地點、B 回時間、C 回人物，皆非所問。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"How long does the flight to Tokyo take?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["Roughly three hours.","At the departure gate.","Two hundred dollars.","Business class."],"a":0,"zh":"飛往東京的航班要多久？→ 大約三小時。","kw":["How long","Tokyo"],"why":"How long 問時間長度，選項 A 回答時長。B 回地點、C 回金額、D 回艙等，都是同為名詞但答非所問。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"When can I pick up the repaired laptop?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["The repair shop is nearby.","The warranty covers a year.","It'll be ready by Friday.","It was a gift."],"a":2,"zh":"我什麼時候可以取回修好的筆電？→ 週五前會修好。","kw":["When","laptop"],"why":"When 問時間，選項 C 給完成時間。A 回地點、B 回保固、D 回來源，皆不回答問題。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"Who called while I was in the meeting?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["In the main conference room.","A representative from the bank.","Around noon.","The report is due Monday."],"a":1,"zh":"我開會時誰打電話來？→ 銀行的一位代表。","kw":["Who","meeting"],"why":"Who 問人物，選項 B 回答打電話的人。A 回地點、C 回時間、D 回截止日，皆為陷阱。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"Why is the conference room unavailable this afternoon?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["Because it's being repainted.","It seats about forty people.","From two to four p.m.","The projector was installed."],"a":0,"zh":"為什麼會議室今天下午不能用？→ 因為正在重新粉刷。","kw":["Why","conference room"],"why":"Why 問原因，選項 A 用 Because 回答原因。B 回容量、C 回時段、D 回設備，都沒有說明不能用的原因。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"How many participants have registered so far?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["Since last Friday.","Via our website.","They are students.","About a hundred and twenty."],"a":3,"zh":"目前有多少人報名？→ 大約一百二十人。","kw":["How many","registered"],"why":"How many 問數量，選項 D 回答人數。A 回時間、B 回方式、C 回身份，皆答非所問。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"What kind of insurance does the company provide?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["It costs fifty dollars a month.","Health and travel coverage.","The premium is due quarterly.","The agent is Ms. Park."],"a":1,"zh":"公司提供什麼種類的保險？→ 健康保險和旅遊保險。","kw":["insurance","company"],"why":"What kind 問種類，選項 B 回答保險類型。A 回保費金額、C 回繳費時間、D 回人物，都是同主題但不對題。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"Is the new software compatible with our system?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["Yes, it works with our latest version.","It was released last month.","The developer is Korean.","The price is reasonable."],"a":0,"zh":"新軟體和我們的系統相容嗎？→ 可以，它與我們最新版本相容。","kw":["compatible","software"],"why":"這是一般問句，問是否相容，選項 A 以 Yes 直接回答。B 回發布時間、C 回開發者、D 回價格，皆非所問。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"Which airline should I take for the connecting flight?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["The flight departs at six.","The gate is B12.","You can transfer with All Nippon Airways.","The fare includes a meal."],"a":2,"zh":"轉機航班該搭哪一家航空公司？→ 可以轉乘全日空。","kw":["Which airline","connecting"],"why":"Which airline 問航空公司，選項 C 回答航空公司。A 回時間、B 回登機門、D 回票價內容，皆答非所問。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"Where did you put the signed contract?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["I signed it this morning.","I filed it in the blue cabinet.","It's for the audit.","My assistant copied it."],"a":1,"zh":"你把簽好的合約放在哪裡？→ 我放在藍色櫃子裡歸檔。","kw":["Where","contract"],"why":"Where 問地點，選項 B 回答存放位置。A 回時間、C 回用途、D 回人物動作，都是陷阱。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"When was the last time the fire alarm was tested?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["Last month, during the inspection.","In the east wing.","By the security team.","Twice a year."],"a":0,"zh":"上次測試火警警報是什麼時候？→ 上個月安檢時。","kw":["When","fire alarm"],"why":"When 問最近一次的時間，選項 A 給出明確時間。C 回執行者看似合理但不是問的重點，B 回地點、D 回頻率，A 最切題。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"How much time do we have before boarding?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["At the international terminal.","For window seats.","Economy class.","About forty minutes."],"a":3,"zh":"登機前我們還有多少時間？→ 大約四十分鐘。","kw":["How much time","boarding"],"why":"How much time 問時間長度，選項 D 回答時間。A 回地點、B 回座位偏好、C 回艙等，皆不對題。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"Who will present the sales figures at the board meeting?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["Since the fiscal year began.","The regional director will.","In the headquarters building.","Over three days."],"a":1,"zh":"誰會在董事會上報告銷售數字？→ 區域總監。","kw":["Who","sales figures"],"why":"Who 問人物，選項 B 回答報告者。A 回時間起點、C 回地點、D 回天數，皆為陷阱。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"What's the weather forecast for the trade show?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["Sunny with a chance of rain.","It starts on Monday.","Near the harbor.","Admission is free."],"a":0,"zh":"商展的天氣預報如何？→ 晴時多雲偶陣雨。","kw":["weather forecast","trade show"],"why":"問天氣預報，選項 A 是天氣內容。B 回時間、C 回地點、D 回門票，皆答非所問。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"Why was the shipment delayed at the port?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["It weighs two tons.","By container ship.","It was held up in customs.","To our warehouse."],"a":2,"zh":"貨運在港口為何延誤？→ 被海關扣留了。","kw":["Why","shipment"],"why":"Why 問原因，選項 C 說被海關卡住即延誤原因。A 回重量、B 回運輸方式、D 回目的地，皆為陷阱。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"How do you like the new office layout?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["It was designed by an architect.","It's much brighter than before.","On the seventh floor.","Last renovated in 2019."],"a":1,"zh":"你覺得新的辦公室格局怎麼樣？→ 比以前明亮多了。","kw":["office layout","like"],"why":"How do you like 問看法，選項 B 表達對新格局的評價。A 回設計者、C 回樓層、D 回翻修年份，都沒有回答喜好。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"Could you let me know your availability next week?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["The meeting room is booked.","My colleague can attend.","The agenda is attached.","I'm free on Tuesday and Wednesday."],"a":3,"zh":"可以告訴我你下週的空檔嗎？→ 我週二和週三有空。","kw":["availability","next week"],"why":"availability 問有空的時間，選項 D 回答可配合的日期。A 回場地、B 回人物、C 回會議資料，皆不對題。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"Which document still needs the manager's signature?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["The purchase order does.","It was filed yesterday.","In the accounting department.","By courier service."],"a":0,"zh":"哪一份文件還需要主管簽名？→ 採購訂單。","kw":["document","signature"],"why":"Which document 問哪份文件，選項 A 指出採購訂單。B 回時間、C 回部門、D 回寄送方式，皆答非所問。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"What time does the shuttle bus leave the hotel?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["It has twelve seats.","The driver is Mr. Kim.","Every half hour, starting at seven.","At the main entrance."],"a":2,"zh":"接駁巴士幾點離開飯店？→ 七點起每半小時一班。","kw":["shuttle bus","leave"],"why":"What time 問時間，選項 C 回答發車時刻。A 回座位數、B 回司機、D 回上車地點，皆為陷阱。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"How did the marketing team reach its sales target?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["In the Asian market.","By launching an online campaign.","Two million dollars.","Ms. Ito led the team."],"a":1,"zh":"行銷團隊如何達成銷售目標？→ 透過推出線上活動。","kw":["marketing team","target"],"why":"How 問達成方式，選項 B 用 By 回答手段。A 回市場、C 回金額、D 回人物，皆答非所問。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"Where can employees get their parking permits renewed?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["At the administration office on the first floor.","Every weekday morning.","For a fee of ten dollars.","Only with a supervisor's approval."],"a":0,"zh":"員工在哪裡可以續辦停車證？→ 一樓的行政辦公室。","kw":["Where","permits"],"why":"Where 問地點，選項 A 給出辦理地點。B 回時間、C 回費用、D 回條件，皆不是地點。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"Who is responsible for booking the venue for the annual dinner?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["The dinner costs eighty dollars a person.","It will be held in June.","Last year's dinner was a success.","Ms. Alvarez in events."],"a":3,"zh":"誰負責訂年終晚宴的場地？→ 活動部門的阿瓦雷斯女士。","kw":["responsible","venue"],"why":"Who 問人物，選項 D 回答負責人。B 回費用、C 回時間、D 以外的同場景資訊皆非人物。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"Why don't we reschedule the interview to Thursday?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["The candidate lives downtown.","That works for me.","The salary is competitive.","The team has five members."],"a":1,"zh":"我們把面試改到週四如何？→ 對我來說可以。","kw":["Thursday","interview"],"why":"這是提議句，選項 B 表示同意是最自然的回應。A 回地點、C 回薪資、D 回團隊人數，皆與提議無關。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 2","audio":"How can I contact the customer service center after hours?","q":"Choose the best response.","o":["They close at six p.m.","The office is downtown.","You can use the 24-hour hotline.","The manager is on duty."],"a":2,"zh":"下班後我要怎麼聯絡客服中心？→ 可以打 24 小時專線。","kw":["customer service","after hours"],"why":"How 問聯絡方式，選項 C 提供管道。A 回營業時間看似相關，但問題問的是下班後如何聯絡，B 回地點、D 回人物也不對。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: Have you finished the quarterly report? M: Not yet. I need the sales figures from the marketing team first.","q":"What does the man mean?","o":["He needs more information.","He has completed the report.","He is on vacation.","He lost the report."],"a":0,"zh":"女：季報寫完了嗎？男：還沒有，我先需要行銷團隊的銷售數據。→ 他還需要更多資訊。","kw":["Not yet","sales figures"],"why":"男士說 Not yet 且還需要銷售數據，代表報告還沒完成、還缺資料，選 A；B 與 Not yet 矛盾。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: I can't believe the printer on the third floor is broken again. M: Don't worry. The maintenance technician is already on his way up.","q":"What will happen next?","o":["The technician will repair the printer.","The woman will buy a new printer.","The man will go to the third floor.","The maintenance office will close."],"a":0,"zh":"女：不敢相信三樓的印表機又壞了。男：別擔心，維修技術員已经在上來的路上了。→ 技術員接下來會來修理印表機。","kw":["on his way","maintenance technician"],"why":"男士說維修技術員 is already on his way up，表示技術員正要來修，選 A；B 買新印表機、D 維修部門關門都未提及，C 男士並未說自己要去三樓。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: The client moved our meeting to the conference room on the first floor. M: Thanks for letting me know. I'll bring the contracts with me.","q":"What will the man do next?","o":["Take the contracts to the meeting.","Cancel the meeting.","Call the client back.","Move to another office."],"a":0,"zh":"女：客戶把我們的會議改到一樓的會議室。男：謝謝你告訴我，我會把合約帶過去。→ 他會帶合約去開會。","kw":["bring the contracts","first floor"],"why":"男士說 I'll bring the contracts with me，代表他下一步是帶合約去一樓開會，選 A；B、C、D 都與他說的話相反或未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: Did you apply for the transfer to the Tokyo branch? M: I'm still thinking about it. The salary is better, but my family doesn't want to move.","q":"What is the man's problem?","o":["He is undecided about moving.","He cannot speak Japanese.","His family already moved to Tokyo.","His application was rejected."],"a":0,"zh":"女：你申請調職到東京分公司了嗎？男：還在考慮，薪水比較好，但家人不想搬家。→ 他還在猶豫要不要搬家。","kw":["still thinking","doesn't want to move"],"why":"男士說 I'm still thinking about it，加上家人不想搬，表示他尚未做決定，選 A；C 說家人已搬走與音檔相反，B、D 均未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: The air conditioning in the meeting room has been fixed. M: Great! I'll tell the design team they can use it this afternoon.","q":"What will the man do?","o":["Inform the design team about the room.","Repair the air conditioner.","Reserve another room.","Cancel the design meeting."],"a":0,"zh":"女：會議室的空調修好了。男：太好了！我會告訴設計團隊今天下午可以使用。→ 他會去通知設計團隊。","kw":["air conditioning","design team"],"why":"男士明說 I'll tell the design team，所以下一步是通知設計團隊，選 A；修空調的是別人，B 不符；C、D 未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: I heard the marketing department is moving to the new building next week. M: Yes, but the finance department will stay here until the renovation is finished.","q":"Where will the finance department be located?","o":["In the new building.","In the current building.","In a temporary office.","Near the marketing department."],"a":1,"zh":"女：聽說行銷部下週要搬到新大樓。男：對，但財務部會留在這裡，直到翻修完成。→ 財務部仍會留在目前的大樓。","kw":["finance department","renovation"],"why":"男士說財務部 will stay here，here 指現在的大樓，選 B；搬到新大樓的是行銷部，A 是聽到行銷部的干擾。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: Why didn't you join the training session yesterday? M: I had to finish the inventory count, so I missed the first half.","q":"What does the man imply?","o":["He was busy with another task.","He disliked the training.","He arrived late to work.","He forgot the session."],"a":0,"zh":"女：你昨天為什麼沒參加訓練課程？男：我得完成庫存盤點，所以錯過了前半段。→ 他當時在忙另一件工作。","kw":["inventory count","missed"],"why":"男士因庫存盤點而錯過課程，表示他被其他工作耽誤，選 A；B 討厭訓練、D 忘記課程都未提及，C 遲到上班也非原因。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: Are we still meeting Mr. Daniels at the hotel at six? M: He just called to say he'd be an hour late because of a flight delay.","q":"What will probably happen?","o":["The meeting will start at seven.","Mr. Daniels will cancel the meeting.","They will change the hotel.","The flight will arrive early."],"a":0,"zh":"女：我們還是在六點跟丹尼爾斯先生在飯店見面嗎？男：他剛打來說會晚一個小時，因為班機延誤。→ 會議將改在七點開始。","kw":["flight delay","an hour late"],"why":"六點加上 an hour late 就是七點，選 A；男士只說晚到，沒說取消或換飯店，B、C 無根據，D 與班機延誤相反。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: Would you like me to proofread the proposal before it goes to the director? M: That would be a great help. I've already checked it twice, but a fresh pair of eyes always helps.","q":"What does the man mean?","o":["He welcomes the woman's review.","He has already sent the proposal.","He thinks the proposal is perfect.","He wants to proofread it himself."],"a":0,"zh":"女：提案送交主管前要我幫你校對嗎？男：那真是幫了大忙，我已經檢查過兩遍，但換個人來看總是好的。→ 他很樂意讓女方幫忙審閱。","kw":["proofread","fresh pair of eyes"],"why":"男士說 fresh pair of eyes always helps，表示他歡迎女方幫忙看，選 A；他說已看過兩遍但不是完美，C 不符，也沒說已送出（B）。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: The new software is much faster, but half the staff hasn't been trained yet. M: That's why the IT department scheduled extra classes for next week.","q":"What is the problem?","o":["Many employees still lack training.","The software is too slow.","The IT department is closed.","The classes were canceled."],"a":0,"zh":"女：新軟體快多了，但有一半員工還沒受訓。男：所以資訊部才安排下週的額外課程。→ 問題是很多員工尚未受訓。","kw":["hasn't been trained","extra classes"],"why":"女說 half the staff hasn't been trained，代表許多人尚未受訓，選 A；B 與 much faster 相反，C、D 都與音檔內容矛盾。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: Did you book the flights for the trade show in Boston? M: Not yet. I'm waiting for the manager to approve the budget.","q":"What is delaying the man?","o":["He is waiting for approval.","He has no budget left.","He has already booked the flights.","The manager is on a trip."],"a":0,"zh":"女：你訂好去波士頓商展的機票了嗎？男：還沒有，我在等經理核准預算。→ 他在等待預算核准。","kw":["Not yet","approve the budget"],"why":"男士說在等 manager to approve the budget，所以延誤原因是等核准，選 A；說預算用完（B）或已訂票（C）都與 Not yet 矛盾，D 未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: I'd like to extend my stay at the conference by two days to attend the workshop. M: You'll need to submit a new travel request to the accounting department.","q":"What should the woman do?","o":["Submit a new travel request.","Leave the conference early.","Pay for the workshop herself.","Ask the workshop organizer."],"a":0,"zh":"女：我想在會議多留兩天參加研討會。男：那你得向會計部門提交一份新的差旅申請。→ 女方應提交新的差旅申請。","kw":["travel request","accounting department"],"why":"男士明確指示要向會計部門 submit a new travel request，選 A；B 提前離開與延長停留相反，C、D 皆未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: The shipment from our supplier hasn't arrived, and the store shelves are almost empty. M: Let's call the express company and ask for the tracking number.","q":"What will the speakers probably do next?","o":["Contact the delivery company.","Close the store.","Order twice as much.","Raise the prices."],"a":0,"zh":"女：供應商的貨還沒到，店裡的貨架幾乎空了。男：我們打給快遞公司問追蹤號碼吧。→ 他們接下來會聯絡運送公司。","kw":["tracking number","express company"],"why":"男士提議打給 express company 要追蹤號碼，所以下一步是聯絡配送公司，選 A；C 加訂、D 漲價、B 關店都未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: Excuse me, Dr. Lewis. Do you have a moment to look at my lab results? M: Of course, Sarah. Bring them over after the lecture.","q":"What is the probable relationship?","o":["Teacher and student.","Doctor and patient.","Manager and employee.","Salesperson and customer."],"a":0,"zh":"女：路易斯博士，有空看一下我的實驗結果嗎？男：當然可以，莎拉，下課後拿過來。→ 兩人是老師與學生的關係。","kw":["Dr. Lewis","lecture"],"why":"對話出現 lecture、lab results，且男方被稱博士並直呼對方名字、要其課後拿來，符合師生關係，選 A；雖有 Dr. 與 lab results，但場景是學校而非醫院，B 是干擾。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: We should grab something to eat before the movie starts. M: There's a nice cafe next to the cinema, but the line is usually long.","q":"Where will the speakers probably go?","o":["A cafe near the cinema.","The cinema's snack bar.","A restaurant downtown.","The man's house."],"a":0,"zh":"女：電影開演前我們先吃點東西吧。男：戲院旁有家不錯的咖啡廳，但通常要排很久。→ 他們可能會去戲院旁的咖啡廳。","kw":["nice cafe","next to the cinema"],"why":"男士推薦 cinema 旁邊的 cafe，因此最可能去那裡，選 A；B 點心吧、C 市中心餐廳、D 男士家都未被提到。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: The boss asked us to submit the weekly figures by Friday noon instead of end of day. M: That gives us only three hours to finish the chart.","q":"What does the man imply?","o":["There is not enough time.","The chart is already finished.","Friday is a holiday.","The boss is on vacation."],"a":0,"zh":"女：老闆要我們週五中午前就交週報數字，而不是下班前。男：這樣我們只有三個小時可以完成圖表。→ 時間不夠。","kw":["Friday noon","three hours"],"why":"中午前截止只剩三小時，男士暗示時間緊迫，選 A；說圖表已完成（B）與 finish the chart 矛盾，C、D 未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: I saw that the elevator is out of order again. M: Yes. Use the stairs on the left if you're going to the fourth floor.","q":"What should the listener do?","o":["Take the stairs on the left to the fourth floor.","Wait for the repair technician.","Use the elevator on the left.","Find an escalator nearby."],"a":0,"zh":"女：我看電梯又故障了。男：對啊，如果你要去四樓，就走左邊的樓梯。→ 應走左邊的樓梯上四樓。","kw":["out of order","the stairs on the left"],"why":"男士指示 Use the stairs on the left，所以要走左邊樓梯，選 A；電梯已 out of order，B 等修好或 C 用電梯都不行，D 扶梯未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: Why did you return the printer cartridge? M: The pages came out faded, and the store replaced it without any problem.","q":"What did the man do?","o":["Exchanged a defective cartridge.","Refilled the cartridge himself.","Bought a new printer.","Complained to the manager."],"a":0,"zh":"女：你為什麼退回印表機墨水匣？男：印出來的頁面顏色淡掉了，店裡毫無問題地幫我換了。→ 他換掉了有瑕疵的墨水匣。","kw":["faded","replaced it"],"why":"印出來 faded，店家 replaced it，代表他把瑕疵品換貨，選 A；B 自行填充、C 買印表機、D 向經理投訴都未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: Have you decided whether to attend the training in Singapore? M: I'd love to, but I can't leave the department during the product launch.","q":"What prevents the man from going?","o":["Work duties during the product launch.","The cost of the trip.","A schedule conflict with the training.","His passport is expired."],"a":0,"zh":"女：你決定要不要參加新加坡的訓練了嗎？男：我很想去，但產品發表期間我不能離開部門。→ 產品發表期的工作職責讓他去不了。","kw":["product launch","can't leave"],"why":"男士說 during the product launch 不能離開部門，原因是發表期的工作，選 A；C 說與訓練時間衝突、B 費用、D 護照都未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: The forecast says it will rain all weekend, so the outdoor event may be moved indoors. M: I'll check with the venue manager this afternoon.","q":"What will the man do?","o":["Discuss the indoor option with the venue manager.","Cancel the outdoor event.","Watch the weather forecast again.","Move to another city."],"a":0,"zh":"女：預報說整個週末都會下雨，戶外活動可能會改到室內。男：我下午去跟場地經理確認。→ 他會和場地經理討論改室內的方案。","kw":["moved indoors","venue manager"],"why":"男士說要 check with the venue manager，所以他會去跟場地經理確認，選 A；取消活動（B）只是女方的推測且男方沒說要取消，C、D 未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: Did you finish reading the memo about the new expense policy? M: Yes. From now on, we have to attach receipts to every claim over fifty dollars.","q":"What is the memo mainly about?","o":["New rules for expense claims.","A raise in employee salaries.","The price of office supplies.","A new accounting software."],"a":0,"zh":"女：你看完關於新差旅報銷政策的備忘錄了嗎？男：看完了，今後五十元以上的申請都要附收據。→ 備忘錄主要講報銷的新規定。","kw":["expense policy","attach receipts"],"why":"主旨題：memo 講 expense policy 且要求附收據，即報銷新規定，選 A；B 加薪、C 辦公用品價格、D 軟體都未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: I'm surprised the new hires finished the orientation a day early. M: They were eager to start on the actual projects.","q":"What does the man say about the new hires?","o":["They were enthusiastic about the work.","They needed more orientation.","They arrived a day late.","They refused the projects."],"a":0,"zh":"女：新進員工提前一天完成職前訓練，真讓我驚訝。男：他們很渴望開始做真正的專案。→ 新進員工對工作很有熱忱。","kw":["eager to start","new hires"],"why":"男士用 eager to start 形容新人，表示他們對工作充滿熱情，選 A；提前完成訓練，所以 B、C 與 a day early 相反，D 未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: Can you send me the revised contract before you leave for the airport? M: I'll email it as soon as the lawyer signs it.","q":"When will the man send the contract?","o":["After the lawyer signs it.","Before leaving the office.","After boarding the plane.","Once the woman replies."],"a":0,"zh":"女：你去機場前可以把修訂後的合約寄給我嗎？男：律師一簽名我就寄電子郵件給你。→ 他會在律師簽名後寄出。","kw":["as soon as","lawyer signs"],"why":"男士說 as soon as the lawyer signs it，條件是律師簽名後，選 A；並未保證在離開辦公室前寄出（B），也與登機、女方回覆無關。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: The restaurant near the station was fully booked, so I made a reservation at the Italian place on Main Street. M: That's fine with me. Their pasta is excellent.","q":"Where will the speakers eat?","o":["At an Italian restaurant on Main Street.","At a restaurant near the station.","At the man's home.","At a cafe on Main Street."],"a":0,"zh":"女：車站附近的餐廳客滿，所以我在主街的義大利餐廳訂了位。男：我沒問題，他們的義大利麵很棒。→ 他們會在主街的義大利餐廳用餐。","kw":["Italian place","Main Street"],"why":"女說明改訂 Main Street 的義大利餐廳，選 A；車站附近那家 fully booked 是陷阱 B，D 的 cafe 未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: I'm worried that the new safety rules will slow down the production line. M: Only for the first week. After that, everyone will be used to them.","q":"What is the woman's concern?","o":["Production may slow down.","The rules are unclear.","Workers may quit.","The line will stop permanently."],"a":0,"zh":"女：我擔心新的安全規則會拖慢生產線。男：只有第一週會這樣，之後大家就習慣了。→ 女方擔心生產變慢。","kw":["slow down","production line"],"why":"女方原話就是 will slow down the production line，選 A；規則不清楚（B）、員工離職（C）、永久停產（D）都不是她的顧慮，D 更與男方保證相反。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: Why did the meeting with the investors end so early? M: They had already reviewed our figures beforehand, so there wasn't much to discuss.","q":"Why did the meeting end early?","o":["The investors were already familiar with the figures.","The investors arrived late.","Our figures were missing.","The presenter was sick."],"a":0,"zh":"女：跟投資人的會議為什麼這麼早就結束？男：他們事先已經看過我們的數字，所以沒什麼好討論的。→ 因為投資人早已熟悉數據。","kw":["reviewed our figures","beforehand"],"why":"男士說他們 beforehand 已 review our figures，所以提早結束，選 A；B、C、D 都與音檔說法不符。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: Do you need help carrying those boxes to the mailroom? M: No, thanks. The cart is right around the corner.","q":"What does the man mean?","o":["He can move the boxes by himself.","He wants the woman to wait.","The mailroom is closed.","The boxes are too heavy."],"a":0,"zh":"女：需要我幫你把這些箱子搬到收發室嗎？男：不用了，謝謝。手推車就在轉角處。→ 他自己搬得動。","kw":["right around the corner","cart"],"why":"男士婉拒帮忙並說有 cart 可用，表示他能自己搬，選 A；若箱子太重（D）就不會拒絕幫忙，B、C 未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: Our competitor just launched a similar product at a lower price. M: Then we should emphasize our after-sales service in the next campaign.","q":"What does the man suggest?","o":["Highlight customer support in their advertising.","Lower their product price.","Stop the next campaign.","Copy the competitor's product."],"a":0,"zh":"女：競爭對手剛以較低價格推出類似產品。男：那我們下次宣傳就該強調售後服務。→ 他建議在廣告中突出客服。","kw":["after-sales service","campaign"],"why":"男士建議在 campaign 中 emphasize after-sales service，即主打客服，選 A；降價（B）是他沒建議的方向，C 停止宣傳、D 抄襲都未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: I can't believe the company is offering free language classes after work hours. M: Me neither. I've already signed up for the German course.","q":"What has the man done?","o":["Registered for a German class.","Taught a language class.","Rejected the company's offer.","Scheduled the classes himself."],"a":0,"zh":"女：真不敢相信公司提供下班後的免費語言課程。男：我也沒想到，我已經報名德文課了。→ 他已經報名德文課程。","kw":["signed up","German course"],"why":"男士說 I've already signed up for the German course，代表已報名，選 A；B 授課、C 拒絕、D 排課都與 signed up 矛盾或未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: The elevator repair crew says the part won't arrive until Thursday. M: Then we'll have to use the freight elevator for the rest of the week.","q":"What is the problem?","o":["A needed part is delayed.","The freight elevator is broken.","The repair crew quit.","Thursday is a holiday."],"a":0,"zh":"女：電梯維修人員說零件要到週四才會到。男：那這週剩下的日子我們只能用貨運電梯。→ 問題是所需零件延遲送達。","kw":["won't arrive","part"],"why":"女說 the part won't arrive until Thursday，即零件延誤是問題所在，選 A；貨運電梯是替代方案而非壞掉（B），C、D 未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: Did you hear that the head office is creating a new customer service team? M: Yes, and they're asking for volunteers from our branch.","q":"What does the man imply?","o":["Employees may be able to join the new team.","The branch will close soon.","Customer complaints are increasing.","The head office needs more money."],"a":0,"zh":"女：你聽說總部要成立新的客服團隊了嗎？男：聽說了，而且他們在向我們分部徵求志願者。→ 員工有可能加入新團隊。","kw":["volunteers","our branch"],"why":"總部向分部徵求 volunteers，暗示員工可以自願加入，選 A；分支機構即將關閉（B）、客訴增加（C）、缺錢（D）都未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: How did the interview go this morning? M: The panel asked about my experience with international projects, and I think I answered well.","q":"What did the man do this morning?","o":["He was interviewed for a position.","He interviewed other candidates.","He presented a project abroad.","He skipped the interview."],"a":0,"zh":"女：今天早上的面試怎麼樣？男：審查委員問了我國際專案的經驗，我覺得答得不錯。→ 他今早參加了求職面試。","kw":["interview","panel"],"why":"男方被 panel 問答，顯示他是被面試者，選 A；B 他面試別人、C 到國外簡報、D 缺席都與 I answered well 矛盾。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: The package was supposed to arrive on Monday, but it's still at the distribution center. M: Let's file a claim with the courier before it gets any later.","q":"What does the man suggest?","o":["Starting a complaint with the delivery company.","Waiting until next week.","Picking up the package himself.","Ordering the item again."],"a":0,"zh":"女：包裹本來週一就該到，現在還在配送中心。男：趁著還沒更晚，我們向快遞公司提出索賠吧。→ 他建議向運送公司投訴索賠。","kw":["file a claim","courier"],"why":"男士提議 file a claim with the courier，即向快遞公司申訴，選 A；C 亲自去取、D 重訂、B 繼續等待都與他的建議不符。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: Why are you taking the rest of the afternoon off? M: I have a dentist appointment, and I've already cleared it with the supervisor.","q":"What will the man do?","o":["See the dentist.","Meet the supervisor.","Work overtime.","Take a business trip."],"a":0,"zh":"女：你下午為什麼要請假？男：我約了牙醫，而且已經跟主管報備過了。→ 他會去看牙醫。","kw":["dentist appointment","supervisor"],"why":"男士說有 dentist appointment，所以下午要去見牙醫，選 A；主管只是已知情（B 不是目的），加班、出差未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 3","audio":"W: The new cafeteria menu has more vegetarian options now. M: I noticed. Even the soups are meat-free on Tuesdays.","q":"What do we learn about the cafeteria?","o":["It serves meat-free dishes on Tuesdays.","It is closed on Tuesdays.","It serves only meat.","It has no vegetarian food."],"a":0,"zh":"女：新菜單現在有更多素食選擇了。男：我注意到了，連週二的湯都是全素的。→ 週二會供應無肉餐點。","kw":["meat-free","Tuesdays"],"why":"男方說 soups are meat-free on Tuesdays，代表週二供應無肉餐，選 A；B 週二公休與音檔相反，C、D 與 vegetarian options 矛盾。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"Attention passengers: Flight 302 to Chicago has been delayed due to bad weather. Please proceed to gate 12 for further information.","q":"What should passengers do?","o":["Go to gate 12","Check in again","Leave the airport","Board immediately"],"a":0,"zh":"廣播：302 班機因惡劣天氣延誤，請到 12 號登機門獲取進一步資訊。→ 旅客應前往 12 號登機門。","kw":["proceed to gate 12","further information"],"why":"廣播請旅客前往 12 號登機門獲取資訊，選 A；班機延誤，所以 D 立刻登機剛好相反。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"You have reached the office of Dr. Ramirez. Our hours are nine a.m. to five p.m., Monday through Friday. Please leave your name and number after the tone, and I will return your call within one business day.","q":"What should the caller do?","o":["Leave a name and phone number.","Call again tomorrow morning.","Visit the office without an appointment.","Wait for an operator to speak."],"a":0,"zh":"您撥的是拉米雷斯醫師辦公室，服務時間為週一至週五上午九點至下午五點。請在嗶聲後留下姓名與電話，我會在一個工作日內回電。→ 來電者應留下姓名與電話。","kw":["leave your name","after the tone"],"why":"語音留言明確指示 leave your name and number after the tone，選 A；B 明天再打、C 未預約前往都與指示不符，D 轉接專員未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"Grand Opening! Sunny Mart, your new supermarket on Elm Street, is offering thirty percent off all fresh produce this weekend. We are open seven days a week from eight a.m. to nine p.m.","q":"What is being advertised?","o":["A supermarket's opening promotion.","A restaurant's new menu.","A street construction project.","A farm's produce delivery service."],"a":0,"zh":"開幕慶！Sunny Mart——榆樹街的新超市，本週末所有新鮮蔬果一律七折。每週營業七天，上午八點至晚上九點。→ 這是一則超市開幕優惠廣告。","kw":["Grand Opening","fresh produce"],"why":"開頭喊出 Grand Opening，內容是超市蔬果折扣，可知是超市開幕促銷，選 A；B 餐廳菜單、C 道路施工、D 農場外送都只是 Elm Street、produce 的字面干擾。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"Attention all staff: the fifth-floor restrooms will be closed for maintenance this Saturday. Please use the facilities on the third floor. We apologize for the inconvenience.","q":"Where should employees go?","o":["The third floor.","The fifth floor.","The basement.","The parking garage."],"a":0,"zh":"全體同仁注意：五樓廁所本週六將封閉維修，請使用三樓的洗手間。造成不便敬請見諒。→ 員工應使用三樓的設施。","kw":["closed for maintenance","third floor"],"why":"公告請員工 use the facilities on the third floor，選 A；五樓是封閉場所，聽到 fifth floor 就選是典型陷阱。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"This is your captain speaking. We expect some turbulence over the next thirty minutes, so please keep your seat belts fastened. Flight attendants, please be seated now.","q":"What are passengers asked to do?","o":["Keep their seat belts fastened.","Move to another seat.","Start the meal service.","Turn off the cabin lights."],"a":0,"zh":"這裡是機長廣播：未來三十分鐘可能會有亂流，請繫好安全帶。空服員請就座。→ 旅客應保持繫上安全帶。","kw":["turbulence","seat belts fastened"],"why":"機長要求 keep your seat belts fastened，選 A；亂流期間送餐、換座位都不宜，C、D 均未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"Tired of waiting for the bus? City Bike Rental now offers monthly passes for only twenty dollars. Download our app, unlock any bike, and ride anywhere in the city.","q":"What can listeners do?","o":["Rent bicycles using a monthly pass.","Buy a city bus ticket.","Purchase a bicycle through the app.","Take a twenty-dollar taxi ride."],"a":0,"zh":"等公車等累了嗎？City Bike Rental 現在推出只要二十元的月票。下載 App、解鎖任一輛單車，就能騎遍全市。→ 聽眾可用月票租借自行車。","kw":["monthly passes","City Bike Rental"],"why":"廣告主打 monthly passes 租車，選 A；App 是用來解鎖不是買車（C），公車票（B）與計程車（D）都是拿 bus、twenty dollars 亂湊的干擾。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"This message is for all parents of Lincoln Middle School students. The field trip to the science museum has been rescheduled to May fifteenth because of the storm. Please sign the new permission form by Monday.","q":"What must parents do?","o":["Sign a new permission form.","Buy museum tickets.","Call the science museum.","Attend a storm meeting."],"a":0,"zh":"這是給林肯中學全體家長的訊息：因暴風雨，科學博物館校外教學已改到五月十五日，請在週一前簽署新的同意書。→ 家長須簽署新的同意書。","kw":["permission form","rescheduled"],"why":"留言最後要求 sign the new permission form by Monday，選 A；買票、致電博物館、開暴風雨會議都未提及，rescheduled 只代表改期。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"Attention shoppers, the store will be closing in fifteen minutes. Please bring your purchases to the checkout lanes now. Thank you for shopping with us.","q":"What should shoppers do?","o":["Go to the checkout lanes now.","Wait outside the store.","Come back tomorrow morning.","Return to their cars."],"a":0,"zh":"各位顧客注意：本店將於十五分鐘後打烊，請現在將購買的商品拿到結帳櫃檯。感謝您的惠顧。→ 顧客應立刻前往結帳。","kw":["closing in fifteen minutes","checkout"],"why":"公告要求 bring your purchases to the checkout lanes now，選 A；C 明天再來、D 回車上都與 now 及即將打烊矛盾。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"Please note that the company parking lot will be repaved next Monday and Tuesday. Employees are advised to use the public garage on Fifth Avenue during that time.","q":"Where should employees park?","o":["The public garage on Fifth Avenue.","The company parking lot.","The lot behind the cafeteria.","The sidewalk on Fifth Avenue."],"a":0,"zh":"請注意：公司停車場下週一、週二將重新鋪路，期間員工請使用第五大道的公共停車場。→ 員工應把車停在第五大道的公共停車場。","kw":["public garage","Fifth Avenue"],"why":"公告建議期間使用 the public garage on Fifth Avenue，選 A；公司停車場正在施工，聽到 company parking lot 就選是陷阱。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"Hello, this is a message from Bright Clean Laundry. Your order will be ready for pickup on Thursday morning instead of Wednesday, since one of our machines was repaired today.","q":"Why is the order delayed?","o":["A machine was repaired.","The customer changed the order.","The store was closed on Wednesday.","Thursday is a holiday."],"a":0,"zh":"您好，這是 Bright Clean 洗衣店的留言：您的訂單將改為週四早上可取件，而非週三，因為我們今天修理了一台機器。→ 延遲原因是機器送修。","kw":["was repaired","instead of Wednesday"],"why":"留言用 since one of our machines was repaired today 解釋改期原因，選 A；B、C、D 都未提及，instead of Wednesday 只代表時間改變。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"Good evening, guests. Our swimming pool will close at nine p.m. tonight for cleaning. The fitness center, however, will remain open until midnight.","q":"What will happen tonight?","o":["The pool will close early for cleaning.","The fitness center will close early.","Both facilities will close at nine.","The hotel will close tonight."],"a":0,"zh":"晚安，各位旅客：游泳池今晚九點將關閉進行清潔，健身中心則營業至午夜。→ 泳池將提早關閉清潔。","kw":["swimming pool","remain open until midnight"],"why":"泳池 nine p.m. 關閉清潔，健身中心 remain open until midnight，選 A；B 與音檔相反，C 說兩者都關、D 說飯店關門都未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"Attention job seekers: Eastside Career Center is offering a free two-week course in computer repair. Classes start on September first, and registration closes this Friday.","q":"What are listeners told to do?","o":["Register by Friday for a free course.","Pay a fee for computer classes.","Visit the center on September first for a tour.","Buy a computer repair kit."],"a":0,"zh":"求職者注意：Eastside 職訓中心提供免費兩週的電腦維修課程，九月一日開課，本週五報名截止。→ 聽眾應在週五前免費報名。","kw":["registration closes","free two-week course"],"why":"課程是 free 且 registration closes this Friday，選 A；B 要付費與 free 相反，C 參觀、D 買工具組均未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"The number seven bus will use a detour until further notice due to road construction on Maple Avenue. Stops along Oak Road will not be served during this period.","q":"What will riders experience?","o":["A changed route until further notice.","The usual stops on Oak Road.","A free bus ride.","A new stop on Oak Road."],"a":0,"zh":"七號公車因楓葉大道道路施工，將改道至另行通知為止，期間橡樹路站牌不會停靠。→ 搭車者會遇到改道。","kw":["detour","road construction"],"why":"公告說 will use a detour until further notice，選 A；橡樹路站牌期間不服務，B、D 都與 will not be served 相反，免費乘車未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"This is Green Valley Clinic calling to remind you of your appointment with Dr. Patel on October twelfth at ten thirty a.m. Please arrive fifteen minutes early to complete your paperwork.","q":"What should the patient do?","o":["Arrive fifteen minutes early.","Bring Dr. Patel's medical records.","Reschedule the appointment.","Complete the paperwork at home."],"a":0,"zh":"這是綠谷診所的來電提醒：您與帕特爾醫師的看診時間是十月十二日上午十點三十分，請提早十五分鐘到場填寫表單。→ 病患應提早十五分鐘到診所。","kw":["fifteen minutes early","appointment"],"why":"診所要求 arrive fifteen minutes early 完成表單，選 A；B 帶病歷、C 改期、D 在家填表都與音檔指示不符。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"Listeners heading downtown should avoid the expressway. A multi-car accident has closed two lanes near the Fourth Street exit, and delays are expected to last another hour.","q":"What does the reporter advise?","o":["Avoid the expressway.","Take the Fourth Street exit.","Expect the delays to end now.","Drive downtown immediately."],"a":0,"zh":"要前往市區的聽眾請避開高速公路：第四街出口附近發生多車事故，封閉兩線道，預計還會壅塞一個小時。→ 建議避開高速公路。","kw":["avoid the expressway","multi-car accident"],"why":"主播直接建議 should avoid the expressway，選 A；第四街出口正是事故處，B 反而會塞車，D 與建議相反。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"Speakers for the afternoon sessions have been moved from Hall A to Hall B. All other presentations will follow the printed schedule.","q":"Where will the afternoon sessions be held?","o":["Hall B.","Hall A.","The registration desk.","The printed schedule room."],"a":0,"zh":"下午場次的講者已從 A 廳改至 B 廳，其餘簡報仍依原印刷時程進行。→ 下午場次在 B 廳。","kw":["Hall B","afternoon sessions"],"why":"公告說 moved from Hall A to Hall B，正確地點是 B 廳，選 A；A 廳是改動前的地點，屬聽到什麼不選什麼的陷阱。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"Try Mama Rossi's new lunch buffet, open weekdays from eleven a.m. to two p.m. All you can eat for just nine dollars, including soup, salad, and dessert.","q":"What is being promoted?","o":["A weekday lunch buffet.","A weekend dinner show.","A cooking class for beginners.","A holiday brunch."],"a":0,"zh":"來試試瑪瑪羅西餐廳的新午餐自助餐：平日上午十一點至下午兩點營業，九元任您享用，附湯、沙拉與甜點。→ 這是在推銷平日午餐自助餐。","kw":["lunch buffet","weekdays"],"why":"廣告主軸是 lunch buffet、weekdays、九元吃到飽，選 A；週末、晚餐秀、料理教學、假日早午餐的時間或內容都與音檔不符。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"Good news, passengers. Flight 415 to Seattle has been upgraded to a larger aircraft, so all checked baggage will be delivered to the carousel within twenty minutes of landing.","q":"What will happen after landing?","o":["Checked baggage will arrive quickly.","The flight will be canceled.","Passengers must check in again.","They will board a smaller aircraft."],"a":0,"zh":"好消息，旅客們：西雅圖 415 航班已改用較大的客機，所有託運行李將在降落后二十分鐘內送到行李轉盤。→ 行李會很快送到。","kw":["checked baggage","within twenty minutes"],"why":"廣播說行李 within twenty minutes of landing 送到轉盤，選 A；B 取消、C 重新報到都未提及，D 與 upgraded to a larger aircraft 相反。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"Staff notice: effective April first, all travel expenses must be submitted through the online system. Paper forms will no longer be accepted.","q":"What has changed?","o":["Expenses must be filed online.","Paper forms are now required.","Travel is prohibited for staff.","The online system will close in April."],"a":0,"zh":"員工通知：自四月一日起，所有差旅費用必須透過線上系統提交，紙本表格不再受理。→ 報銷改為線上提交。","kw":["online system","Paper forms"],"why":"公告要求 through the online system，且 Paper forms will no longer be accepted，選 A；B 與後半句正好相反，C、D 未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"This is a reminder from the Water Department. Due to scheduled pipe work, residents on Birch Lane will experience low water pressure on Thursday morning. Please store enough water in advance.","q":"What should residents do?","o":["Store water in advance.","Move out of Birch Lane.","Call a private plumber.","Boil water all day Thursday."],"a":0,"zh":"這是水務局的提醒：因計畫性管線工程，樺樹巷居民週四上午水壓偏低，請事先儲水。→ 居民應提前儲水。","kw":["low water pressure","store enough water"],"why":"公告請居民 store enough water in advance，選 A；B 搬家、C 找私人水電、D 全天煮水都未提及，低水壓只需備水。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"Hi, this is Mark in accounting. The quarterly budget meeting has been moved to Room 305. Also, don't forget to bring the updated spreadsheets.","q":"What does Mark want the listener to know?","o":["The meeting room has changed.","The budget has been cut.","The spreadsheets are missing.","He will not attend the meeting."],"a":0,"zh":"嗨，我是會計部的馬克：季度預算會議已改到 305 室，另外別忘了帶更新過的試算表。→ 他要告知會議地點改了。","kw":["Room 305","updated spreadsheets"],"why":"留言重點是 has been moved to Room 305，即會議室變更，選 A；預算被砍、試算表遺失、他不出席都未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"New members are reminded that the group yoga class on Wednesday evenings is now limited to twenty participants. Please reserve your spot at the front desk.","q":"What must members do?","o":["Reserve a place in advance.","Bring their own yoga mats.","Arrive an hour early.","Cancel the Wednesday class."],"a":0,"zh":"提醒新會員：週三晚間的團體瑜伽課現限額二十人，請到櫃檯預留名額。→ 會員須事先預約名額。","kw":["reserve your spot","twenty participants"],"why":"公告要求 reserve your spot at the front desk，選 A；自備瑜珈墊、提早一小時、取消課程都未提及，limited to twenty 只是名額限制。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"Moving soon? QuickMove offers same-day delivery of small furniture within the city for a flat fee of thirty-five dollars. Book online or call our twenty-four-hour line.","q":"What service does QuickMove provide?","o":["Same-day delivery of small furniture.","Long-distance moving trucks.","Free packing boxes.","Twenty-four-hour guided tours."],"a":0,"zh":"快要搬家了嗎？QuickMove 提供市內小型家具當天送達，固定收費三十五元，可線上預約或撥打二十四小時專線。→ 它提供小型家具當日配送服務。","kw":["same-day delivery","QuickMove"],"why":"廣告主打 same-day delivery of small furniture，選 A；B 長途卡車、C 免費紙箱、D 導覽都是拿 booking、twenty-four-hour 誤導的選項。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"The city's annual outdoor concert has been postponed until next Friday because of high winds. Ticket holders may keep their tickets for the new date or request a refund.","q":"What can ticket holders do?","o":["Keep their tickets or request a refund.","Get free tickets for tonight.","Attend the concert tonight.","Exchange tickets for parking."],"a":0,"zh":"本市年度戶外音樂會因強風延期至下週五，持票者可保留票券改期使用或申請退費。→ 持票者可保留票券或退費。","kw":["postponed","refund"],"why":"公告給持票者兩個選擇 keep their tickets or request a refund，選 A；C 今晚參加與 postponed 矛盾，B、D 未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"Ladies and gentlemen, the museum will close in thirty minutes. For your safety, please begin moving toward the east exit. Large bags must be checked at the cloakroom.","q":"What are visitors asked to do?","o":["Leave through the east exit.","Check in their coats only.","Stay for another hour.","Move toward the west exit."],"a":0,"zh":"各位貴賓：博物館將於三十分鐘後閉館，為您的安全請開始往東側出口移動，大件行李須寄放在衣帽間。→ 訪客應由東側出口離開。","kw":["east exit","thirty minutes"],"why":"公告要求 move toward the east exit，選 A；D 西側出口方向相反，B 只寄外套不完整（是大件行李必寄），C 與三十分鐘後閉館矛盾。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"Looking for office furniture? DeskWorld's fall sale starts today. Desks and chairs are up to forty percent off, and delivery is free for orders over one hundred dollars.","q":"What is being advertised?","o":["A furniture sale with free delivery over one hundred dollars.","A new office building for rent.","A discount on computers and printers.","An electronics clearance event."],"a":0,"zh":"在找辦公家具嗎？DeskWorld 秋季特賣今天開跑，桌椅最高六折，訂購滿一百元免運費。→ 這是家具特賣且滿額免運的廣告。","kw":["DeskWorld","delivery is free"],"why":"內容是桌椅折扣加 free delivery for orders over one hundred dollars，選 A；C 電腦、D 電子清倉都與家具不符，B 租辦公室未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"Passengers on flight two hundred eighteen to Toronto, please proceed to gate nine for boarding. Due to the large crowd, we ask that you have your boarding passes ready.","q":"What should these passengers do?","o":["Go to gate nine with boarding passes ready.","Change their flight to Toronto.","Check in their luggage again.","Wait in the departure lounge."],"a":0,"zh":"飛往多倫多的 218 航班旅客，請前往九號登機門登機，因人潮眾多，請備妥登機證。→ 旅客應帶好登機證前往九號登機門。","kw":["gate nine","boarding passes"],"why":"廣播指示 proceed to gate nine for boarding，且 boarding passes ready，選 A；改航班、再次托運行李、在候機室等待都與登機指示不符。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"Hello, this is your building manager. The water will be turned off on Wednesday from nine a.m. to noon for pipe replacement. Please plan accordingly.","q":"What will happen on Wednesday?","o":["Water will be unavailable in the morning.","The pipes will be installed for the first time.","The building will be sold.","The manager will move out."],"a":0,"zh":"您好，我是大樓管理員：週三上午九點至中午將因更換管線而停水，請提早因應。→ 週三上午將停水。","kw":["water will be turned off","pipe replacement"],"why":"留言說 water will be turned off from nine a.m. to noon，即上午無水可用，選 A；pipe replacement 是更換不是首次安裝（B），C、D 未提及。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"Reminder: the annual company picnic will be held at Riverside Park this Saturday instead of the office lawn. Lunch will be served at noon, and shuttle buses leave the main entrance at ten.","q":"Where will the picnic be held?","o":["At Riverside Park.","At the office lawn.","At the main entrance.","At a downtown restaurant."],"a":0,"zh":"提醒：年度公司野餐本週六將於河濱公園舉行，而非辦公室草坪。中午供應午餐，接駁車十點從大門發車。→ 地點在河濱公園。","kw":["Riverside Park","shuttle buses"],"why":"公告明說 will be held at Riverside Park instead of the office lawn，選 A；B 是原地點的陷阱，C 大門只是上車處。"},{"t":"listen","part":"Part 4","audio":"This is the school library. The book you requested, Ocean Science Today, is ready for pickup. Please return any overdue items at the same time.","q":"What should the listener do?","o":["Pick up the requested book and return overdue items.","Buy Ocean Science Today for class.","Wait for another book request.","Donate old books to the library."],"a":0,"zh":"這裡是學校圖書館：您預約的《今日海洋科學》已可領取，同時請歸還任何逾期未還的圖書。→ 領書並歸還逾期圖書。","kw":["ready for pickup","overdue items"],"why":"留言同時提到 ready for pickup 與 return any overdue items，選 A；買書、等待新預約、捐書都未提及。"}],"read":[{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"Sales representatives are expected to arrive at the office ______ every morning.","o":["punctual","punctuality","punctually","punctuate"],"a":2,"zh":"業務代表每天早晨應準時到辦公室；修飾動詞 arrive 需用副詞 punctually。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The company recorded a ______ increase in international sales this quarter.","o":["significant","significantly","significance","signify"],"a":0,"zh":"公司本季海外銷售顯著成長；名詞 increase 之前需用形容詞 significant。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The hotel provides a free ______ service for all overnight guests.","o":["laundry","laundrying","laundries","launder"],"a":0,"zh":"飯店為住宿客人提供免費洗衣服務；空格需名詞 laundry，其餘詞性不符。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"Please ______ the report to the sales director before Friday.","o":["submit","submits","submitting","submitted"],"a":0,"zh":"請在週五前把報告提交給銷售主管；祈使句用原形動詞 submit。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"______ you please forward me the updated contact list?","o":["Would","Does","Are","Is"],"a":0,"zh":"麻煩你轉寄最新的聯絡人名單好嗎？you 之後的請求句用 Would you please。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"______ most popular item on our website last month was the wireless keyboard.","o":["A","An","The","—"],"a":2,"zh":"上個月網站上最受歡迎的商品是無線鍵盤；最高級 most popular 前須用定冠詞 the。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The finance manager is responsible ______ the company's annual budget.","o":["for","with","of","at"],"a":0,"zh":"財務經理負責公司的年度預算；be responsible for 為固定用法。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"We look forward to hearing ______ you soon.","o":["from","to","with","by"],"a":0,"zh":"期待很快收到你的來信；hear from（收到某人的消息）為固定搭配。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"We look forward to ______ your reply at your earliest convenience.","o":["receive","receiving","received","receives"],"a":1,"zh":"期待您盡快回覆；look forward to 的 to 是介系詞，後接 V-ing。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The Finance Director asked ______ to prepare the quarterly report.","o":["I","me","myself","mine"],"a":1,"zh":"財務長要我準備季報；asked 之後作受詞用受格 me。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"John and ______ will represent the company at the trade fair.","o":["I","me","myself","mine"],"a":0,"zh":"約翰和我將代表公司參加展覽；位於主詞位置用主格 I。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"Is this umbrella yours or ______?","o":["my","mine","me","myself"],"a":1,"zh":"這把雨傘是你的還是我的？yours 之後須用名詞性物主代名詞 mine。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"Look! The children ______ in the playground.","o":["play","are playing","played","have played"],"a":1,"zh":"看！孩子們正在操場上玩；Look! 提示此刻動作，用現在進行式。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"It is important for all employees ______ the safety regulations.","o":["follow","following","to follow","followed"],"a":2,"zh":"所有員工遵守安全規定很重要；句型 It is + 形容詞 + for + 受詞 + to V。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The manager insisted ______ paying for the entire meal.","o":["on","at","to","for"],"a":0,"zh":"經理堅持要付整餐的錢；insist on + V-ing 為固定用法。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"Employees must complete the annual safety training ______.","o":["annual","annually","annualize","annuals"],"a":1,"zh":"員工必須每年完成安全訓練；修飾動詞 complete 用副詞 annually。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The new software ______ every employee to access files from any location.","o":["enable","enables","enabling","are enabled"],"a":1,"zh":"新軟體讓每位員工都能從任何地點存取檔案；單數主詞用第三人稱單數 enables。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"Could you please ______ me your calculator for a moment?","o":["lend","borrow","borrowing","lending"],"a":0,"zh":"可以借我計算機一下嗎？lend 某人某物＝借出；borrow 是「借入」，不能加人作受詞。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The lawyer ______ us not to sign the revised contract yet.","o":["advise","advice","advises","advising"],"a":2,"zh":"律師建議我們先別簽修訂後的合約；第三人稱單數用 advises，advice 是名詞。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The hotel offers ______ views of the coastline from every room.","o":["stunning","stunningly","stun","stunned"],"a":0,"zh":"飯店每間房都能看到絕美的海岸景觀；名詞 views 之前需用形容詞 stunning。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The committee will ______ a final decision by the end of the week.","o":["make","makes","making","made"],"a":0,"zh":"委員會將在本週結束前做出最終決定；will 之後接原形動詞 make。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The marketing team ______ a new campaign next month.","o":["launch","launches","launching","launched"],"a":1,"zh":"行銷團隊下個月將推出新活動；單數主詞 team 用第三人稱單數現在式表未來安排。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"If it ______ tomorrow, the baseball game will be canceled.","o":["rains","will rain","rained","has rained"],"a":0,"zh":"明天下雨的話棒球賽將取消；if 引導的條件句用現在式代替未來式，不可用 will。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"Please make sure to sign ______ each page of the contract.","o":["on","at","in","of"],"a":0,"zh":"請確認在合約每一頁上簽名；sign on each page（在每頁上簽名）。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"______ the heavy rain, the outdoor event proceeded as planned.","o":["Despite","Although","Because","Unless"],"a":0,"zh":"儘管下著大雨，戶外活動仍照常舉行；Despite 是介系詞，後接名詞片語 the heavy rain。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The manager could not attend the meeting ______ he was traveling abroad.","o":["because","because of","despite","in spite of"],"a":0,"zh":"經理因為出國而無法出席會議；because 後接完整子句，because of 後接名詞片語。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The manager suggested ______ the meeting until next Monday.","o":["to postpone","postponing","postpone","postponed"],"a":1,"zh":"經理建議把會議延到下週一；suggest 後接 V-ing，不用 to V。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"My colleagues and I prepared the entire presentation ______; no outside help was needed.","o":["ourselves","ourself","themselves","us"],"a":0,"zh":"我和同事們自己完成了整份簡報；主詞含 I，反身代名詞用 ourselves。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The quality of the product did not live ______ to our customers' expectations.","o":["up","on","at","for"],"a":0,"zh":"產品品質沒有達到客戶的期望；live up to＝不辜負、達到。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The new tax policy had an immediate ______ on the housing market.","o":["affect","effect","effective","affected"],"a":1,"zh":"新稅制對房市產生立即影響；had an effect on 為名詞用法，affect 是動詞。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"Each of the applicants ______ to submit two letters of recommendation.","o":["have","has","having","are having"],"a":1,"zh":"每位申請者都須提交兩封推薦信；each of + 複數名詞，動詞用單數 has。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The company ______ a new warehouse in Kaohsiung since 2023.","o":["has built","built","builds","is building"],"a":0,"zh":"公司自 2023 年起在高雄興建新倉庫；since + 時間點須用現在完成式。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The employee ______ won the annual award will be promoted next month.","o":["who","whom","whose","which"],"a":0,"zh":"獲頒年度獎的員工下月將升遷；關係代名詞在子句中作受詞動詞 won 的主詞，用 who。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"______ of the sudden increase in demand, the factory hired twenty more workers.","o":["Because","Despite","Although","Even"],"a":0,"zh":"由於需求突然增加，工廠多雇了二十名員工；because of + 名詞片語，Despite of 為錯誤用法。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The new policy takes effect ______ January 1, 2027.","o":["on","at","of","to"],"a":0,"zh":"新政策將於 2027 年 1 月 1 日生效；具體日期前面用介系詞 on。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The intern avoided ______ personal emails during office hours.","o":["to send","sending","sent","sends"],"a":1,"zh":"實習生避免在上班時間寄私人電子郵件；avoid 後接 V-ing。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"Sales of the new product ______ by 15 percent last quarter.","o":["rose","raised","rise","aroused"],"a":0,"zh":"新產品上季銷售額成長 15%；rise 為不及物動詞用過去式 rose，raise 需接受詞。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"Ms. Wong ______ in the finance department for over a decade, and she has no plans to retire.","o":["worked","has worked","works","is working"],"a":1,"zh":"黃女士在財務部任職十多年且沒有退休計畫；for + 一段時間須用現在完成式。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The number of job applicants ______ increasing every year.","o":["is","are","were","have"],"a":0,"zh":"求職者的人數逐年增加；the number of + 複數名詞，動詞用單數 is。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"______ the fact that the flight was delayed, we still made it to the ceremony on time.","o":["Despite","Although","Because","Unless"],"a":0,"zh":"儘管班機延誤，我們仍準時抵達典禮；despite the fact that 後接名詞片語，Although 後須接完整子句。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The prize was presented to the winner by ______.","o":["he","him","his","himself"],"a":1,"zh":"獎項頒給了得獎者；介系詞 by 之後用受格 him，反身代名詞需與主詞同指。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"Please ______ that all doors are locked before you leave the building.","o":["assure","ensure","insure","ensuring"],"a":1,"zh":"離開大樓前請確認所有門都已上鎖；ensure＝確保，assure 後接人，insure＝投保。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The committee agreed ______ the proposal at the next meeting.","o":["discussing","to discuss","discuss","discussed"],"a":1,"zh":"委員會同意在下次會議討論提案；agree 後接 to + 原形動詞。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"By the time we arrived, the meeting ______ already ______.","o":["has...begun","had...begun","will...begin","is...beginning"],"a":1,"zh":"我們抵達時會議已經開始；過去完成式表示「過去的過去」。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The auditors ______ the books when the fire alarm went off.","o":["examine","were examining","have examined","will examine"],"a":1,"zh":"火警響起時稽核人員正在查帳；when + 過去式子句，主句用過去進行式。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"______ John nor Maria has signed the employment contract yet.","o":["Neither","Either","Both","Whether"],"a":0,"zh":"約翰和瑪莉亞都還沒簽雇用合約；neither...nor 搭配，動詞與就近的 Maria 一致用單數。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"Not only ______ the report late, but he also forgot to attach the supporting data.","o":["did he submit","he did submit","he submitted","he has submitted"],"a":0,"zh":"他不僅交報告遲了，還忘了附上佐證資料；not only 置於句首時主詞與助動詞要倒裝。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"Not only the employees but also the manager ______ responsible for the error.","o":["are","is","were","have been"],"a":1,"zh":"不只員工，經理也對錯誤負責；not only...but also 依就近原則，與單數 the manager 一致用 is。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"You may invite ______ your brother or your sister to the company dinner.","o":["either","both","neither","whether"],"a":0,"zh":"你可以邀請你弟弟或妹妹參加公司聚餐；either...or 為固定相關詞。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"Neither the manager nor the assistants ______ available to answer the phone this afternoon.","o":["is","are","was being","has been"],"a":1,"zh":"經理和助理今天下午都沒空接電話；neither...nor 依就近原則，與複數 assistants 一致用 are。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"A number of employees ______ submitted complaints about the new policy.","o":["has","have","is having","having"],"a":1,"zh":"不少員工已經對新政策提出申訴；a number of＝許多，動詞用複數 have。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The list of required documents ______ been updated by the human resources department.","o":["have","has","having","are"],"a":1,"zh":"所需文件清單已由人資部更新；主詞是單數 list，of 後的名詞不影響動詞。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The construction of the new bridge ______ next March.","o":["completes","will complete","is completed","will be completed"],"a":3,"zh":"新橋工程將於明年三月完工；主詞是動作的承受者，用未來式被動 will be completed。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The window in the conference room needs ______.","o":["repairing","to repair","repair","repaired"],"a":0,"zh":"會議室的窗戶需要修理；need + V-ing 表被動（＝needs to be repaired），to repair 語意不通。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"Please remain seated ______ the airplane has come to a complete stop.","o":["until","during","throughout","among"],"a":0,"zh":"請留在座位上直到飛機完全停妥；until 後接子句，during/throughout 後只接名詞片語。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"______ you submit your application by March 31, it will not be processed.","o":["Unless","Despite","During","Owing to"],"a":0,"zh":"除非你在 3 月 31 日前提出申請，否則將不予受理；Unless＝if...not，後接完整子句。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The shipment was delayed ______ the severe weather conditions.","o":["due to","because","owing","accordance"],"a":0,"zh":"貨運因惡劣天氣延誤；due to + 名詞片語，because 後須接子句、owing 後須接 to。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The new regulation will ______ the way companies report their earnings.","o":["effect","affect","affects","effective"],"a":1,"zh":"新法規將影響企業申報獲利的方式；will 後用動詞原形 affect，effect 通常作名詞。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The new furniture is a perfect ______ to the office décor.","o":["complement","compliment","complementary","completely"],"a":0,"zh":"新家具與辦公室裝潢十分相襯；complement＝補充、相配，compliment＝讚美。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 5","q":"The auditors had barely begun their work ______ the fire alarm went off.","o":["when","than","despite","because of"],"a":0,"zh":"稽核人員才剛開始工作，火警就響了；had barely...when＝剛一…就…，其餘選項後不能接完整子句。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"Dear Ms. Liu,\nThank you for your application for the marketing position at our company. We would like to invite you for a(n) ______ on Thursday, March 12, at 10:00 a.m. Please bring a copy of your ______, because our managers would like to see your previous work. The interview will last about 45 minutes in Room 201. If this time does not ______ you, please contact our office by Monday, March 9. We look forward to meeting you soon.\nSincerely,\nHR Department","q":"The company would like to invite Ms. Liu for a(n) ______ on March 12.","o":["interview","invoice","discount","survey"],"a":0,"zh":"信中邀請劉小姐於3月12日參加面試，interview 意為「面試」。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"Dear Ms. Liu,\nThank you for your application for the marketing position at our company. We would like to invite you for a(n) ______ on Thursday, March 12, at 10:00 a.m. Please bring a copy of your ______, because our managers would like to see your previous work. The interview will last about 45 minutes in Room 201. If this time does not ______ you, please contact our office by Monday, March 9. We look forward to meeting you soon.\nSincerely,\nHR Department","q":"Ms. Liu should bring a copy of her ______ to show her previous work.","o":["purchase","portfolio","postage","postcard"],"a":1,"zh":"信中要求攜帶作品集（portfolio），以展示過去的作品。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"Dear Ms. Liu,\nThank you for your application for the marketing position at our company. We would like to invite you for a(n) ______ on Thursday, March 12, at 10:00 a.m. Please bring a copy of your ______, because our managers would like to see your previous work. The interview will last about 45 minutes in Room 201. If this time does not ______ you, please contact our office by Monday, March 9. We look forward to meeting you soon.\nSincerely,\nHR Department","q":"If the time does not ______ Ms. Liu, she should contact the office by Monday.","o":["seat","save","suit","seek"],"a":2,"zh":"若時間不合適（not suit you），請於週一前聯絡公司。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"Attention all staff:\nOur office will move to the ______ floor of the Riverside Building on Saturday, June 6. All computers and files must be ______ into boxes by Friday afternoon, because the movers will not handle loose items. The moving company will ______ the boxes at 9:00 a.m. on Saturday, so please keep the hallway clear. Your new desks and chairs are already in place, and you can start work as usual on Monday. If you have any questions, please contact Ms. Chen in Administration.\nAdministration Department","q":"The office is moving to the ______ floor of the Riverside Building.","o":["five","fifty","fifteen","fifth"],"a":3,"zh":"辦公室將搬至五樓，表示樓層須用序數詞 fifth。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"Attention all staff:\nOur office will move to the ______ floor of the Riverside Building on Saturday, June 6. All computers and files must be ______ into boxes by Friday afternoon, because the movers will not handle loose items. The moving company will ______ the boxes at 9:00 a.m. on Saturday, so please keep the hallway clear. Your new desks and chairs are already in place, and you can start work as usual on Monday. If you have any questions, please contact Ms. Chen in Administration.\nAdministration Department","q":"Computers and files must be ______ into boxes before Friday afternoon.","o":["printed","packed","painted","posted"],"a":1,"zh":"電腦與文件須在週五下午前裝箱（packed into boxes）。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"Attention all staff:\nOur office will move to the ______ floor of the Riverside Building on Saturday, June 6. All computers and files must be ______ into boxes by Friday afternoon, because the movers will not handle loose items. The moving company will ______ the boxes at 9:00 a.m. on Saturday, so please keep the hallway clear. Your new desks and chairs are already in place, and you can start work as usual on Monday. If you have any questions, please contact Ms. Chen in Administration.\nAdministration Department","q":"The moving company will ______ the boxes at 9:00 a.m. on Saturday.","o":["confirm","correct","collect","connect"],"a":2,"zh":"搬家公司週六早上會來收（collect）紙箱。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"Dear Mr. Park,\nThank you for your order of 200 office chairs placed on May 3. The total amount is $6,400, and delivery is ______ for May 20; the truck has already been booked. As requested, we will send the chairs to your warehouse in Busan instead of the head office. Please check the ______ attached to this email and pay within 30 days. If you need to have the delivery date ______, please let us know at least three days in advance so that we can inform the factory.\nBest regards,\nSeoul Office Supply Co.","q":"Delivery of the chairs is ______ for May 20.","o":["scheduled","suggested","separated","suspended"],"a":0,"zh":"交貨已排定（scheduled for）於5月20日，貨車也已訂好。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"Dear Mr. Park,\nThank you for your order of 200 office chairs placed on May 3. The total amount is $6,400, and delivery is ______ for May 20; the truck has already been booked. As requested, we will send the chairs to your warehouse in Busan instead of the head office. Please check the ______ attached to this email and pay within 30 days. If you need to have the delivery date ______, please let us know at least three days in advance so that we can inform the factory.\nBest regards,\nSeoul Office Supply Co.","q":"Mr. Park should check the ______ attached to the email and pay within 30 days.","o":["invitation","inventory","invoice","investment"],"a":2,"zh":"信中要求核對隨信附上的發票（invoice）並於30天內付款。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"Dear Mr. Park,\nThank you for your order of 200 office chairs placed on May 3. The total amount is $6,400, and delivery is ______ for May 20; the truck has already been booked. As requested, we will send the chairs to your warehouse in Busan instead of the head office. Please check the ______ attached to this email and pay within 30 days. If you need to have the delivery date ______, please let us know at least three days in advance so that we can inform the factory.\nBest regards,\nSeoul Office Supply Co.","q":"If the delivery date needs to be ______, the factory must be informed three days ahead.","o":["charged","checked","changed","chartered"],"a":2,"zh":"若交貨日期需要更改（changed），須提前三天通知工廠。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"Dear Passenger,\nPlease note that Flight NH 842 from Tokyo to Singapore on July 15 has been ______. The plane will now depart at 2:30 p.m. instead of 11:00 a.m. because of a runway repair at Narita Airport. Passengers who cannot make the new departure time may request a full ______ or transfer to another flight without paying any extra ______. Please arrive at the airport at least two hours before departure. For more information, please visit our website or contact the reservation desk at the airport.\nNippon Airways","q":"Because of a runway repair, Flight NH 842 on July 15 has been ______.","o":["reserved","rescheduled","reviewed","reduced"],"a":1,"zh":"跑道維修導致航班改期（rescheduled），起飛時間由上午11點改為下午2點半。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"Dear Passenger,\nPlease note that Flight NH 842 from Tokyo to Singapore on July 15 has been ______. The plane will now depart at 2:30 p.m. instead of 11:00 a.m. because of a runway repair at Narita Airport. Passengers who cannot make the new departure time may request a full ______ or transfer to another flight without paying any extra ______. Please arrive at the airport at least two hours before departure. For more information, please visit our website or contact the reservation desk at the airport.\nNippon Airways","q":"Passengers who cannot take the new flight may request a full ______.","o":["refund","referee","reference","reform"],"a":0,"zh":"無法配合新時間的旅客可申請全額退款（refund）。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"Dear Passenger,\nPlease note that Flight NH 842 from Tokyo to Singapore on July 15 has been ______. The plane will now depart at 2:30 p.m. instead of 11:00 a.m. because of a runway repair at Narita Airport. Passengers who cannot make the new departure time may request a full ______ or transfer to another flight without paying any extra ______. Please arrive at the airport at least two hours before departure. For more information, please visit our website or contact the reservation desk at the airport.\nNippon Airways","q":"Passengers can transfer to another flight without paying any extra ______.","o":["chance","chart","charge","check"],"a":2,"zh":"改搭其他航班不需額外收費（extra charge）。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"Hello Daniel,\nI have ______ two rooms at the Grand Plaza Hotel for the sales conference on October 8 and 9. The rooms are on the sixth floor and face the garden. Breakfast is ______ in the rate, but dinner must be paid separately. Check-in ______ at 3:00 p.m., and the hotel offers free parking for all guests. The conference room we reserved is next to the elevator, and the hotel will provide coffee and tea free of charge during the sessions. Please send me your arrival time so that I can inform the front desk.\nBest,\nMaria","q":"Maria has ______ two rooms for the sales conference.","o":["broken","booked","built","brought"],"a":1,"zh":"Maria 已為研討會訂了（booked）兩間客房。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"Hello Daniel,\nI have ______ two rooms at the Grand Plaza Hotel for the sales conference on October 8 and 9. The rooms are on the sixth floor and face the garden. Breakfast is ______ in the rate, but dinner must be paid separately. Check-in ______ at 3:00 p.m., and the hotel offers free parking for all guests. The conference room we reserved is next to the elevator, and the hotel will provide coffee and tea free of charge during the sessions. Please send me your arrival time so that I can inform the front desk.\nBest,\nMaria","q":"Breakfast is ______ in the room rate.","o":["included","increased","indicated","intended"],"a":0,"zh":"房價已包含（included in）早餐，晚餐則需另付。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"Hello Daniel,\nI have ______ two rooms at the Grand Plaza Hotel for the sales conference on October 8 and 9. The rooms are on the sixth floor and face the garden. Breakfast is ______ in the rate, but dinner must be paid separately. Check-in ______ at 3:00 p.m., and the hotel offers free parking for all guests. The conference room we reserved is next to the elevator, and the hotel will provide coffee and tea free of charge during the sessions. Please send me your arrival time so that I can inform the front desk.\nBest,\nMaria","q":"Check-in at the Grand Plaza Hotel ______ at 3:00 p.m.","o":["belongs","benefits","behaves","begins"],"a":3,"zh":"飯店下午3點開始（begins）辦理住房登記。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"To: All Customer Service Staff\nFrom: Training Office\nSubject: Afternoon Workshop on September 20\nA half-day workshop on handling difficult customers will be held in Room 302 from 1:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m. Attendance is ______ for all new employees. Please ______ your attendance by September 15 through the company website. Staff who attend the full session will receive a ______ at the end of the workshop. This training replaces the session originally planned for September 13. Please note that latecomers will not be admitted after 1:15 p.m.\nTraining Office","q":"All new employees are ______ to attend the workshop.","o":["required","reduced","recorded","retired"],"a":0,"zh":"所有新員工都必須（required）參加，出勤為強制性。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"To: All Customer Service Staff\nFrom: Training Office\nSubject: Afternoon Workshop on September 20\nA half-day workshop on handling difficult customers will be held in Room 302 from 1:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m. Attendance is ______ for all new employees. Please ______ your attendance by September 15 through the company website. Staff who attend the full session will receive a ______ at the end of the workshop. This training replaces the session originally planned for September 13. Please note that latecomers will not be admitted after 1:15 p.m.\nTraining Office","q":"Employees must ______ their attendance by September 15.","o":["confide","conflict","confirm","combine"],"a":2,"zh":"請於9月15日前透過公司網站確認（confirm）出席。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"To: All Customer Service Staff\nFrom: Training Office\nSubject: Afternoon Workshop on September 20\nA half-day workshop on handling difficult customers will be held in Room 302 from 1:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m. Attendance is ______ for all new employees. Please ______ your attendance by September 15 through the company website. Staff who attend the full session will receive a ______ at the end of the workshop. This training replaces the session originally planned for September 13. Please note that latecomers will not be admitted after 1:15 p.m.\nTraining Office","q":"Participants will receive a ______ at the end of the workshop.","o":["celebration","certificate","condition","conversation"],"a":1,"zh":"全程參加者在研討會結束時會獲得證書（certificate）。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"Travel Policy Update\nEffective January 1, all employees must use the online ______ system for flights and hotels. Printed tickets will no longer be accepted at the airport. Economy class is required for flights under six hours, while business class ______ approval from your department manager. Receipts must be ______ within five business days of your trip. Any expense that is not entered in the system within this period will require written explanation from your manager. Employees who submit late receipts may be reimbursed only two weeks later.\nFinance Department","q":"All employees must use the online ______ system for travel bookings.","o":["baking","booking","broadcasting","building"],"a":1,"zh":"新規定要求員工使用線上訂位（booking）系統訂機票與飯店。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"Travel Policy Update\nEffective January 1, all employees must use the online ______ system for flights and hotels. Printed tickets will no longer be accepted at the airport. Economy class is required for flights under six hours, while business class ______ approval from your department manager. Receipts must be ______ within five business days of your trip. Any expense that is not entered in the system within this period will require written explanation from your manager. Employees who submit late receipts may be reimbursed only two weeks later.\nFinance Department","q":"Business class ______ approval from a department manager.","o":["requires","refuses","reserves","reduces"],"a":0,"zh":"商務艙需要（requires）部門主管核准。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"Travel Policy Update\nEffective January 1, all employees must use the online ______ system for flights and hotels. Printed tickets will no longer be accepted at the airport. Economy class is required for flights under six hours, while business class ______ approval from your department manager. Receipts must be ______ within five business days of your trip. Any expense that is not entered in the system within this period will require written explanation from your manager. Employees who submit late receipts may be reimbursed only two weeks later.\nFinance Department","q":"Receipts must be ______ within five business days of the trip.","o":["underlined","uploaded","upgraded","understood"],"a":1,"zh":"收據須在五個工作日內上傳（uploaded）到系統。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"Our quarterly sales report shows that online sales ______ by 18 percent in the third quarter, while store sales remained almost unchanged. The main ______ for the increase was a new advertising campaign launched in August. The report also notes that returns fell by four percent, which suggests that customers are more satisfied with the products they buy online. Although shipping costs went up, our overall profit still improved because customers ordered more items per transaction. We recommend ______ the campaign into the next year and opening two more stores in the suburbs.\nMarketing Division","q":"According to the report, online sales ______ by 18 percent in the third quarter.","o":["raised","raising","rose","rises"],"a":2,"zh":"線上銷售上升18%，不及物動詞 rise 的過去式為 rose。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"Our quarterly sales report shows that online sales ______ by 18 percent in the third quarter, while store sales remained almost unchanged. The main ______ for the increase was a new advertising campaign launched in August. The report also notes that returns fell by four percent, which suggests that customers are more satisfied with the products they buy online. Although shipping costs went up, our overall profit still improved because customers ordered more items per transaction. We recommend ______ the campaign into the next year and opening two more stores in the suburbs.\nMarketing Division","q":"The main ______ for the sales increase was a new advertising campaign.","o":["result","reason","reward","revenge"],"a":1,"zh":"銷售增長的主要原因（reason for）是八月推出的新廣告活動。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"Our quarterly sales report shows that online sales ______ by 18 percent in the third quarter, while store sales remained almost unchanged. The main ______ for the increase was a new advertising campaign launched in August. The report also notes that returns fell by four percent, which suggests that customers are more satisfied with the products they buy online. Although shipping costs went up, our overall profit still improved because customers ordered more items per transaction. We recommend ______ the campaign into the next year and opening two more stores in the suburbs.\nMarketing Division","q":"The Marketing Division recommends ______ the campaign next year.","o":["continued","continuation","continue","continuing"],"a":3,"zh":"recommend 後接動名詞，應為 continuing the campaign。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"Dear Ms. Alvarez,\nFurther to our telephone conversation, I am attaching the revised contract for your review. Clause 4 has been ______ to state that payment will be made in two ______ rather than one. The delivery date remains unchanged at November 30. Kindly sign the document and return a ______ copy to our legal department by October 12. Should you wish to discuss any of the terms, my assistant can arrange a call with you this week.\nYours faithfully,\nThomas Reed, Legal Advisor","q":"Clause 4 of the contract has been ______.","o":["accused","achieved","amended","accessed"],"a":2,"zh":"第4條已被修訂（amended），付款方式改為兩期。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"Dear Ms. Alvarez,\nFurther to our telephone conversation, I am attaching the revised contract for your review. Clause 4 has been ______ to state that payment will be made in two ______ rather than one. The delivery date remains unchanged at November 30. Kindly sign the document and return a ______ copy to our legal department by October 12. Should you wish to discuss any of the terms, my assistant can arrange a call with you this week.\nYours faithfully,\nThomas Reed, Legal Advisor","q":"Payment will be made in two ______ rather than one.","o":["installments","installations","instruments","invitations"],"a":0,"zh":"合約規定分兩期（installments）付款，而非一次付清。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"Dear Ms. Alvarez,\nFurther to our telephone conversation, I am attaching the revised contract for your review. Clause 4 has been ______ to state that payment will be made in two ______ rather than one. The delivery date remains unchanged at November 30. Kindly sign the document and return a ______ copy to our legal department by October 12. Should you wish to discuss any of the terms, my assistant can arrange a call with you this week.\nYours faithfully,\nThomas Reed, Legal Advisor","q":"Ms. Alvarez should return a ______ copy of the signed contract.","o":["scattered","scheduled","scanned","squeezed"],"a":2,"zh":"請簽名後回傳掃描（scanned）副本給法務部門。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"When the Riverfront Mall opened in 2019, few people ______ that it would become the busiest shopping center in the region. Its success was largely due to the decision to ______ the top floor for restaurants and a small cinema rather than for more shops. This layout encourages visitors to stay longer, and many of them spend money on levels they would otherwise pass through quickly. Competitors have since attempted to ______ the idea, but none has matched the mall's visitor numbers.\nBusiness Weekly","q":"When the mall opened, few people ______ that it would become the busiest in the region.","o":["preferred","predicted","protested","prohibited"],"a":1,"zh":"幾乎沒有人預料（predicted）到它會成為最熱鬧的購物中心。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"When the Riverfront Mall opened in 2019, few people ______ that it would become the busiest shopping center in the region. Its success was largely due to the decision to ______ the top floor for restaurants and a small cinema rather than for more shops. This layout encourages visitors to stay longer, and many of them spend money on levels they would otherwise pass through quickly. Competitors have since attempted to ______ the idea, but none has matched the mall's visitor numbers.\nBusiness Weekly","q":"The top floor was ______ for restaurants and a cinema.","o":["resolve","respond","reserve","retire"],"a":2,"zh":"頂樓被保留（reserved for）給餐廳與小型電影院，而非更多商店。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 6","passage":"When the Riverfront Mall opened in 2019, few people ______ that it would become the busiest shopping center in the region. Its success was largely due to the decision to ______ the top floor for restaurants and a small cinema rather than for more shops. This layout encourages visitors to stay longer, and many of them spend money on levels they would otherwise pass through quickly. Competitors have since attempted to ______ the idea, but none has matched the mall's visitor numbers.\nBusiness Weekly","q":"Competitors have tried to ______ the mall's idea.","o":["indicate","intimate","imitate","irritate"],"a":2,"zh":"競爭對手試圖模仿（imitate）這個構想，但無人能及。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"GRAND OPENING SPECIAL\nBella's Kitchen - Italian Restaurant\n120 King Street, Downtown\nTo celebrate our opening, all customers receive 20% off their total bill from November 3 to November 10. Our menu features homemade pasta, wood-fired pizza, and fresh salads made with local vegetables. We are open from 11:00 a.m. to 10:00 p.m. every day of the week. Reservations are recommended for groups of six or more. Please mention this advertisement to your server when you order.\nFor bookings, call (02) 5550-1188.","q":"What is the main purpose of the advertisement?","o":["To announce the closing of a restaurant","To invite customers to try a new restaurant","To explain a menu price increase","To apply for a restaurant job"],"a":1,"zh":"這是新餐廳開幕優惠廣告，目的是吸引顧客嚐鮮。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"GRAND OPENING SPECIAL\nBella's Kitchen - Italian Restaurant\n120 King Street, Downtown\nTo celebrate our opening, all customers receive 20% off their total bill from November 3 to November 10. Our menu features homemade pasta, wood-fired pizza, and fresh salads made with local vegetables. We are open from 11:00 a.m. to 10:00 p.m. every day of the week. Reservations are recommended for groups of six or more. Please mention this advertisement to your server when you order.\nFor bookings, call (02) 5550-1188.","q":"How much do customers save during the promotion period?","o":["10 percent","15 percent","20 percent","25 percent"],"a":2,"zh":"開幕期間全單打8折，即享有20%折扣。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"GRAND OPENING SPECIAL\nBella's Kitchen - Italian Restaurant\n120 King Street, Downtown\nTo celebrate our opening, all customers receive 20% off their total bill from November 3 to November 10. Our menu features homemade pasta, wood-fired pizza, and fresh salads made with local vegetables. We are open from 11:00 a.m. to 10:00 p.m. every day of the week. Reservations are recommended for groups of six or more. Please mention this advertisement to your server when you order.\nFor bookings, call (02) 5550-1188.","q":"For which customers are reservations recommended?","o":["Groups of six or more","Single diners","Takeout customers","Staff members"],"a":0,"zh":"廣告建議6人以上團體先訂位。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"From: Lisa Grant <lisa.grant@northgate.com>\nTo: All Staff\nSubject: Meeting Room 4B - Temporary Closure\nPlease be advised that Meeting Room 4B will be closed for painting on Friday, September 12. The room will reopen on Monday, September 15, at 9:00 a.m. During this time, please book Room 2A or Room 5C for any meetings. Reservations can be made through the office calendar system as usual. We are sorry for any inconvenience.\nFacilities Team","q":"Why will Meeting Room 4B be unavailable on September 12?","o":["It will be painted","It will be moved","It will be used for training","It will be locked for a fire drill"],"a":0,"zh":"9月12日會議室4B要粉刷，因此暫時關閉。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"From: Lisa Grant <lisa.grant@northgate.com>\nTo: All Staff\nSubject: Meeting Room 4B - Temporary Closure\nPlease be advised that Meeting Room 4B will be closed for painting on Friday, September 12. The room will reopen on Monday, September 15, at 9:00 a.m. During this time, please book Room 2A or Room 5C for any meetings. Reservations can be made through the office calendar system as usual. We are sorry for any inconvenience.\nFacilities Team","q":"When can staff use Meeting Room 4B again?","o":["On Friday, September 12","On Saturday, September 13","On Monday, September 15","On September 30"],"a":2,"zh":"郵件寫明9月15日（週一）上午9點重新開放。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"From: Lisa Grant <lisa.grant@northgate.com>\nTo: All Staff\nSubject: Meeting Room 4B - Temporary Closure\nPlease be advised that Meeting Room 4B will be closed for painting on Friday, September 12. The room will reopen on Monday, September 15, at 9:00 a.m. During this time, please book Room 2A or Room 5C for any meetings. Reservations can be made through the office calendar system as usual. We are sorry for any inconvenience.\nFacilities Team","q":"How can employees reserve another room?","o":["By calling the facilities team","Through the office calendar system","By emailing Ms. Grant personally","At the front desk on the ground floor"],"a":1,"zh":"預約仍透過公司日曆系統（office calendar system）辦理。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"TOKYO - OSAKA EXPRESS TIMETABLE (Weekdays)\nTrain No. 701  Dep. 6:15 a.m.  Arr. 8:30 a.m.  Non-stop\nTrain No. 705  Dep. 7:40 a.m.  Arr. 10:05 a.m.  Stops at Nagoya\nTrain No. 711  Dep. 9:20 a.m.  Arr. 11:45 a.m.  Non-stop\nTrain No. 719  Dep. 12:10 p.m.  Arr. 2:35 p.m.  Stops at Nagoya\n* Tickets must be purchased before boarding. Bicycles and large luggage are not allowed on these trains.","q":"Which train arrives in Osaka at 10:05 a.m.","o":["Train No. 701","Train No. 705","Train No. 711","Train No. 719"],"a":1,"zh":"時刻表顯示705號列車於上午10:05抵達大阪。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"TOKYO - OSAKA EXPRESS TIMETABLE (Weekdays)\nTrain No. 701  Dep. 6:15 a.m.  Arr. 8:30 a.m.  Non-stop\nTrain No. 705  Dep. 7:40 a.m.  Arr. 10:05 a.m.  Stops at Nagoya\nTrain No. 711  Dep. 9:20 a.m.  Arr. 11:45 a.m.  Non-stop\nTrain No. 719  Dep. 12:10 p.m.  Arr. 2:35 p.m.  Stops at Nagoya\n* Tickets must be purchased before boarding. Bicycles and large luggage are not allowed on these trains.","q":"What are passengers told before they board?","o":["They must buy tickets in advance","They may bring bicycles on board","They can pay on the train","Large luggage is free of charge"],"a":0,"zh":"附註說明上車前必須先買票（tickets must be purchased before boarding）。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"SEASIDE RESORT - SUMMER SPECIAL\nEscape to the Seaside Resort this summer! Stay three nights or more and get the fourth night free. The package includes breakfast for two, free Wi-Fi, and access to the indoor pool. Check-in is at 2:00 p.m. and check-out is at 11:00 a.m. The offer is valid from June 1 to August 31 and cannot be combined with other promotions. Book online at www.seasideresort.com or call our reservation desk. Children under 12 stay free in the same room.","q":"What is included in the package?","o":["Dinner for two","Breakfast for two","Airport transfers","A free city tour"],"a":1,"zh":"方案包含兩人份早餐（breakfast for two）、免費Wi-Fi與室內泳池。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"SEASIDE RESORT - SUMMER SPECIAL\nEscape to the Seaside Resort this summer! Stay three nights or more and get the fourth night free. The package includes breakfast for two, free Wi-Fi, and access to the indoor pool. Check-in is at 2:00 p.m. and check-out is at 11:00 a.m. The offer is valid from June 1 to August 31 and cannot be combined with other promotions. Book online at www.seasideresort.com or call our reservation desk. Children under 12 stay free in the same room.","q":"What must guests do to receive the free night?","o":["Book online","Bring children under 12","Stay at least three nights","Arrive before 2:00 p.m."],"a":2,"zh":"住滿三晚以上才能享有第四晚免費。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"SEASIDE RESORT - SUMMER SPECIAL\nEscape to the Seaside Resort this summer! Stay three nights or more and get the fourth night free. The package includes breakfast for two, free Wi-Fi, and access to the indoor pool. Check-in is at 2:00 p.m. and check-out is at 11:00 a.m. The offer is valid from June 1 to August 31 and cannot be combined with other promotions. Book online at www.seasideresort.com or call our reservation desk. Children under 12 stay free in the same room.","q":"When can the offer NOT be used?","o":["During another promotion","On weekdays","In June","For families with children"],"a":0,"zh":"優惠有效期為6/1至8/31，且不可與其他促銷活動併用。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"PART-TIME POSITION AVAILABLE\nGreenfield Bookstore is looking for a part-time sales assistant for the holiday season. Working hours are 12:00 p.m. to 8:00 p.m., Tuesday to Sunday. Duties include arranging displays, answering customer questions, and operating the cash register. No experience is necessary, but applicants must enjoy working with people and be able to stand for long periods. The pay is $16 an hour. Please send your resume to jobs@greenfieldbooks.com by November 30.\nGreenfield Bookstore, 88 Lake Road","q":"Which task is mentioned in the advertisement?","o":["Delivering books to customers' homes","Writing book reviews for a website","Operating the cash register","Managing staff schedules"],"a":2,"zh":"工作內容包含擺設陳列、回答顧客問題與操作收銀機。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"PART-TIME POSITION AVAILABLE\nGreenfield Bookstore is looking for a part-time sales assistant for the holiday season. Working hours are 12:00 p.m. to 8:00 p.m., Tuesday to Sunday. Duties include arranging displays, answering customer questions, and operating the cash register. No experience is necessary, but applicants must enjoy working with people and be able to stand for long periods. The pay is $16 an hour. Please send your resume to jobs@greenfieldbooks.com by November 30.\nGreenfield Bookstore, 88 Lake Road","q":"What is true about the working hours?","o":["They run from noon to 8:00 p.m., Tuesday to Sunday","They are from 8:00 a.m. to noon, Monday to Friday","They are overnight shifts","They are only on Sundays"],"a":0,"zh":"上班時間為週二至週日中午12點到晚上8點。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"PART-TIME POSITION AVAILABLE\nGreenfield Bookstore is looking for a part-time sales assistant for the holiday season. Working hours are 12:00 p.m. to 8:00 p.m., Tuesday to Sunday. Duties include arranging displays, answering customer questions, and operating the cash register. No experience is necessary, but applicants must enjoy working with people and be able to stand for long periods. The pay is $16 an hour. Please send your resume to jobs@greenfieldbooks.com by November 30.\nGreenfield Bookstore, 88 Lake Road","q":"How should interested people apply?","o":["Visit the store in the morning","Call before December 1","Send a resume by November 30","Complete a form at the cash register"],"a":2,"zh":"應徵者須在11月30日前將履歷寄到指定信箱。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"RIVERSIDE COMMUNITY GROUP - Posted October 4\nHi neighbors! Our annual charity book sale is back. This year it will be held in the community hall on Saturday, October 18, from 9:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m. We are collecting used books until October 15, so please drop them off at the library front desk. All money raised will go to the local children's hospital. We still need five volunteers to help set up tables on Friday evening. Please comment below if you can help!","q":"What is the group asking residents to donate?","o":["Used books","New computers","Cash only","Volunteer fees"],"a":0,"zh":"社團正在收集舊書（used books），10月15日前可放到圖書館櫃台。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"RIVERSIDE COMMUNITY GROUP - Posted October 4\nHi neighbors! Our annual charity book sale is back. This year it will be held in the community hall on Saturday, October 18, from 9:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m. We are collecting used books until October 15, so please drop them off at the library front desk. All money raised will go to the local children's hospital. We still need five volunteers to help set up tables on Friday evening. Please comment below if you can help!","q":"What will happen to the money raised?","o":["It will be shared among volunteers","It will go to a children's hospital","It will pay for the community hall","It will buy new books for the library"],"a":1,"zh":"義賣所得將全數捐給當地兒童醫院。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"RIVERSIDE COMMUNITY GROUP - Posted October 4\nHi neighbors! Our annual charity book sale is back. This year it will be held in the community hall on Saturday, October 18, from 9:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m. We are collecting used books until October 15, so please drop them off at the library front desk. All money raised will go to the local children's hospital. We still need five volunteers to help set up tables on Friday evening. Please comment below if you can help!","q":"What do the organizers still need?","o":["A new venue","Five people to set up tables","A sponsor for the event","More books after October 18"],"a":1,"zh":"主辦單位還需要5名志工協助週五晚間擺桌。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"PRODUCT SAFETY NOTICE\nModel: K-Tech Kettle K100\nSold from March 1 to May 20\nK-Tech has discovered that the handle of the K100 kettle may become loose after repeated use, which could cause hot water to spill. No injuries have been reported so far. Customers who own this model should stop using it immediately and contact our service center for a free repair or a full refund. The serial number is printed on the bottom of the kettle. For assistance, call 1-800-555-0199 or visit k-tech.com/recall.\nK-Tech Customer Care","q":"What is the purpose of the notice?","o":["To warn customers about a possible safety problem","To advertise a new kettle model","To explain how to use the K100","To apologize for a delayed delivery"],"a":0,"zh":"公告指出K100熱水壺把手可能鬆脫，屬安全警告。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"PRODUCT SAFETY NOTICE\nModel: K-Tech Kettle K100\nSold from March 1 to May 20\nK-Tech has discovered that the handle of the K100 kettle may become loose after repeated use, which could cause hot water to spill. No injuries have been reported so far. Customers who own this model should stop using it immediately and contact our service center for a free repair or a full refund. The serial number is printed on the bottom of the kettle. For assistance, call 1-800-555-0199 or visit k-tech.com/recall.\nK-Tech Customer Care","q":"What should owners of the kettle do?","o":["Keep using it carefully","Return it to the store for a discount","Stop using it and contact the service center","Register it online for a warranty extension"],"a":2,"zh":"擁有者應立即停止使用並聯絡客服中心，可免費維修或全額退款。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"PRODUCT SAFETY NOTICE\nModel: K-Tech Kettle K100\nSold from March 1 to May 20\nK-Tech has discovered that the handle of the K100 kettle may become loose after repeated use, which could cause hot water to spill. No injuries have been reported so far. Customers who own this model should stop using it immediately and contact our service center for a free repair or a full refund. The serial number is printed on the bottom of the kettle. For assistance, call 1-800-555-0199 or visit k-tech.com/recall.\nK-Tech Customer Care","q":"Where is the serial number located?","o":["On the handle","On the bottom of the kettle","On the receipt","In the user manual"],"a":1,"zh":"序號印在水壺底部（bottom of the kettle）。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"INTERNAL MEMO\nTo: All Department Heads\nFrom: IT Services\nDate: July 9\nSubject: Printer Replacement on Floors 2 and 3\nThe old printers on floors 2 and 3 will be replaced with new network models during the weekend of July 18-19. From Monday, July 20, all print jobs must be sent to the new printers. Before then, staff must install a new printer driver on their computers; step-by-step instructions are attached to this memo. Old printer codes will stop working on July 17. If you experience any problems, please submit a ticket through the IT help desk.","q":"What must staff do before using the new printers?","o":["Install a new printer driver","Buy new paper","Move to a different floor","Submit a ticket to the IT help desk"],"a":0,"zh":"備忘錄要求員工先安裝新的印表機驅動程式（printer driver）。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"INTERNAL MEMO\nTo: All Department Heads\nFrom: IT Services\nDate: July 9\nSubject: Printer Replacement on Floors 2 and 3\nThe old printers on floors 2 and 3 will be replaced with new network models during the weekend of July 18-19. From Monday, July 20, all print jobs must be sent to the new printers. Before then, staff must install a new printer driver on their computers; step-by-step instructions are attached to this memo. Old printer codes will stop working on July 17. If you experience any problems, please submit a ticket through the IT help desk.","q":"When will the old printer codes stop working?","o":["On July 9","On July 17","On July 18","On July 20"],"a":1,"zh":"舊的列印代碼將於7月17日失效。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"INTERNAL MEMO\nTo: All Department Heads\nFrom: IT Services\nDate: July 9\nSubject: Printer Replacement on Floors 2 and 3\nThe old printers on floors 2 and 3 will be replaced with new network models during the weekend of July 18-19. From Monday, July 20, all print jobs must be sent to the new printers. Before then, staff must install a new printer driver on their computers; step-by-step instructions are attached to this memo. Old printer codes will stop working on July 17. If you experience any problems, please submit a ticket through the IT help desk.","q":"When will the new printers be installed?","o":["On July 9","On July 17","Over the weekend of July 18-19","On Monday, July 20"],"a":2,"zh":"新印表機將於7月18至19日的週末期間安裝。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"Hi Robert,\nHere is the plan for the trade fair in Berlin. Our flight, LH204, leaves Heathrow at 7:15 a.m. on Monday, October 6, and arrives at 9:30 a.m. A company car will meet you at the airport. We are staying at the Hotel Mitte, where your reservation is under the name 'R. Thompson' for three nights. The fair opens at 10:00 a.m. on Tuesday, and our booth is in Hall C, stand number 42. Please bring 500 product brochures with you.\nSee you at the gate,\nAnna","q":"How will Robert get from the airport?","o":["By hotel shuttle","By company car","By train","By taxi at his own expense"],"a":1,"zh":"Anna 會派公司車到機場接 Robert。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"Hi Robert,\nHere is the plan for the trade fair in Berlin. Our flight, LH204, leaves Heathrow at 7:15 a.m. on Monday, October 6, and arrives at 9:30 a.m. A company car will meet you at the airport. We are staying at the Hotel Mitte, where your reservation is under the name 'R. Thompson' for three nights. The fair opens at 10:00 a.m. on Tuesday, and our booth is in Hall C, stand number 42. Please bring 500 product brochures with you.\nSee you at the gate,\nAnna","q":"Under which name is the hotel room reserved?","o":["Anna Thompson","Hotel Mitte","Robert Reed","R. Thompson"],"a":3,"zh":"飯店訂房登記的名字是 R. Thompson。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"Hi Robert,\nHere is the plan for the trade fair in Berlin. Our flight, LH204, leaves Heathrow at 7:15 a.m. on Monday, October 6, and arrives at 9:30 a.m. A company car will meet you at the airport. We are staying at the Hotel Mitte, where your reservation is under the name 'R. Thompson' for three nights. The fair opens at 10:00 a.m. on Tuesday, and our booth is in Hall C, stand number 42. Please bring 500 product brochures with you.\nSee you at the gate,\nAnna","q":"What must Robert bring with him?","o":["500 product brochures","A taxi receipt","The booth key","Three nights' payment"],"a":0,"zh":"Anna 要求 Robert 準備500份產品手冊。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"Many office workers believe that a long lunch break makes them less productive, but research suggests the opposite. A study of 600 employees found that those who took a proper break away from their desks returned to work with more energy and made fewer errors. Interestingly, the length of the break mattered less than the activity: workers who walked outside or chatted with colleagues reported greater benefits than those who continued working while eating at their desks. The authors therefore recommend that companies actively encourage staff to leave their desks during the lunch hour.\nSource: Workplace Health Journal, May issue","q":"What did the study find about employees who took proper breaks?","o":["They made fewer mistakes","They worked longer hours","They ate at their desks","They received higher pay"],"a":0,"zh":"研究發現離開座位好好休息的員工回工作崗位後犯錯較少。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"Many office workers believe that a long lunch break makes them less productive, but research suggests the opposite. A study of 600 employees found that those who took a proper break away from their desks returned to work with more energy and made fewer errors. Interestingly, the length of the break mattered less than the activity: workers who walked outside or chatted with colleagues reported greater benefits than those who continued working while eating at their desks. The authors therefore recommend that companies actively encourage staff to leave their desks during the lunch hour.\nSource: Workplace Health Journal, May issue","q":"According to the study, what mattered more than the length of the break?","o":["The time of day","The cost of the meal","What employees did during it","Where the company is located"],"a":2,"zh":"休息時間長短不如休息時從事的活動重要。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"Many office workers believe that a long lunch break makes them less productive, but research suggests the opposite. A study of 600 employees found that those who took a proper break away from their desks returned to work with more energy and made fewer errors. Interestingly, the length of the break mattered less than the activity: workers who walked outside or chatted with colleagues reported greater benefits than those who continued working while eating at their desks. The authors therefore recommend that companies actively encourage staff to leave their desks during the lunch hour.\nSource: Workplace Health Journal, May issue","q":"What do the authors recommend?","o":["Shortening the lunch hour","Encouraging staff to leave their desks","Allowing employees to work while eating","Offering free meals in the office"],"a":1,"zh":"作者建議公司鼓勵員工午餐時間離開座位。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"Dear Customer Services,\nI am writing to complain about order number 4482, which arrived on September 2. Three of the twelve chairs were damaged in transit, and one was missing completely. I telephoned your office on September 3 and was told that a replacement would be sent within five working days, but nothing has arrived. As we need the chairs for a conference on September 20, I would appreciate delivery by September 15 at the latest. Otherwise, I would like a full refund for the missing chair.\nYours faithfully,\nHelen Okafor, Events Manager, Brightline Ltd.","q":"What problem is the writer reporting?","o":["The wrong chairs were delivered","Some chairs were damaged and one is missing","The delivery arrived a month late","The invoice was sent to the wrong address"],"a":1,"zh":"12張椅子中3張在運送中損壞、1張完全遺失。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"Dear Customer Services,\nI am writing to complain about order number 4482, which arrived on September 2. Three of the twelve chairs were damaged in transit, and one was missing completely. I telephoned your office on September 3 and was told that a replacement would be sent within five working days, but nothing has arrived. As we need the chairs for a conference on September 20, I would appreciate delivery by September 15 at the latest. Otherwise, I would like a full refund for the missing chair.\nYours faithfully,\nHelen Okafor, Events Manager, Brightline Ltd.","q":"What did the company promise on September 3?","o":["To send a replacement within five working days","To offer a discount on the next order","To collect the damaged chairs immediately","To confirm the conference date"],"a":0,"zh":"9月3日電話中公司承諾5個工作日內補寄，但至今未到。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"Dear Customer Services,\nI am writing to complain about order number 4482, which arrived on September 2. Three of the twelve chairs were damaged in transit, and one was missing completely. I telephoned your office on September 3 and was told that a replacement would be sent within five working days, but nothing has arrived. As we need the chairs for a conference on September 20, I would appreciate delivery by September 15 at the latest. Otherwise, I would like a full refund for the missing chair.\nYours faithfully,\nHelen Okafor, Events Manager, Brightline Ltd.","q":"What does the writer want if the chairs do not arrive in time?","o":["A new order at half price","A full refund for the missing chair","An apology by email","A free conference ticket"],"a":1,"zh":"若無法準時送達，她要求對遺失的那張椅子全額退款。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"Although passenger numbers at regional airports have grown steadily since 2021, many of the smaller airports continue to lose money. The main difficulty is that airlines prefer to concentrate their flights on a few large hubs, where they can fill bigger planes more easily. Regional authorities have responded by offering subsidies to carriers that operate routes to smaller towns. Early results are promising: one airport in the north reported a 27 percent rise in passengers after a subsidy was introduced. However, critics argue that public money would be better spent on improving rail links.\nFinancial Times, March 12","q":"Why do airlines prefer large hubs?","o":["They can fill larger planes more easily","They pay no landing fees","They receive government subsidies","They are closer to regional towns"],"a":0,"zh":"航空公司偏好大型樞紐，因為較容易讓大飛機坐滿。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"Although passenger numbers at regional airports have grown steadily since 2021, many of the smaller airports continue to lose money. The main difficulty is that airlines prefer to concentrate their flights on a few large hubs, where they can fill bigger planes more easily. Regional authorities have responded by offering subsidies to carriers that operate routes to smaller towns. Early results are promising: one airport in the north reported a 27 percent rise in passengers after a subsidy was introduced. However, critics argue that public money would be better spent on improving rail links.\nFinancial Times, March 12","q":"How have regional authorities tried to attract flights?","o":["By raising ticket prices","By improving rail links","By offering subsidies","By building bigger hubs"],"a":2,"zh":"地方當局以補貼（subsidies）吸引航空公司開闢小鎮航線。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"Although passenger numbers at regional airports have grown steadily since 2021, many of the smaller airports continue to lose money. The main difficulty is that airlines prefer to concentrate their flights on a few large hubs, where they can fill bigger planes more easily. Regional authorities have responded by offering subsidies to carriers that operate routes to smaller towns. Early results are promising: one airport in the north reported a 27 percent rise in passengers after a subsidy was introduced. However, critics argue that public money would be better spent on improving rail links.\nFinancial Times, March 12","q":"What do critics believe the public money should be spent on?","o":["Subsidizing more airlines","Improving rail links","Expanding regional airports","Promoting air travel"],"a":1,"zh":"批評者主張公共資金應用於改善鐵路連結（rail links）。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"From: j.mori@globalfreight.co.jp\nTo: s.diaz@vantage-retail.com\nSubject: RE: Container Shipment VN-221\nHi Sofia,\nThe container is now on the vessel Pacific Star, which departed Yokohama on April 4 and is due to arrive in Long Beach on April 18. Customs clearance usually takes two working days, so the goods should be ready for collection on April 22. Please arrange the truck by then, because the terminal charges an extra fee for storage after five days. I have attached the bill of lading and the packing list for your records.\nBest regards,\nJun Mori","q":"When should the goods be ready for collection?","o":["On April 4","On April 18","On April 20","On April 22"],"a":3,"zh":"貨船4月18日抵港，報關約需兩個工作日，4月22日即可提貨。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"From: j.mori@globalfreight.co.jp\nTo: s.diaz@vantage-retail.com\nSubject: RE: Container Shipment VN-221\nHi Sofia,\nThe container is now on the vessel Pacific Star, which departed Yokohama on April 4 and is due to arrive in Long Beach on April 18. Customs clearance usually takes two working days, so the goods should be ready for collection on April 22. Please arrange the truck by then, because the terminal charges an extra fee for storage after five days. I have attached the bill of lading and the packing list for your records.\nBest regards,\nJun Mori","q":"Why should the truck be arranged by April 22?","o":["The terminal adds storage fees after five days","The vessel leaves on that day","Customs officers work only on Mondays","The bill of lading expires"],"a":0,"zh":"貨櫃碼頭超過五天會加收倉儲費，因此須準時安排卡車。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"When the city council announced plans to close the Riverside swimming pool last year, residents reacted with surprise and anger. Built in 1974, the pool had been used by schools and sports clubs for decades, and many families depended on it for affordable exercise. The council argued that repairs to the leaking roof would cost more than the pool could earn in entrance fees. In response, a local campaign group collected 4,200 signatures and organized a swim-in on a cold Sunday morning. Since then, the council has agreed to keep the pool open until at least 2028 while it looks for a private operator to take over its management.","q":"Why did the council want to close the pool?","o":["It was too old to be used","Repairs would cost more than the income it produced","Local families opposed it","Schools refused to pay fees"],"a":1,"zh":"市議會認為屋頂維修費會高於門票收入，因此想關閉泳池。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"When the city council announced plans to close the Riverside swimming pool last year, residents reacted with surprise and anger. Built in 1974, the pool had been used by schools and sports clubs for decades, and many families depended on it for affordable exercise. The council argued that repairs to the leaking roof would cost more than the pool could earn in entrance fees. In response, a local campaign group collected 4,200 signatures and organized a swim-in on a cold Sunday morning. Since then, the council has agreed to keep the pool open until at least 2028 while it looks for a private operator to take over its management.","q":"How did residents respond to the announcement?","o":["They signed a petition and held a swim-in","They voted out the council members","They stopped using the pool","They asked schools to take over"],"a":0,"zh":"居民發起連署（4,200個簽名）並舉辦泳池快閃活動以示抗議。"},{"t":"read","part":"Part 7","passage":"When the city council announced plans to close the Riverside swimming pool last year, residents reacted with surprise and anger. Built in 1974, the pool had been used by schools and sports clubs for decades, and many families depended on it for affordable exercise. The council argued that repairs to the leaking roof would cost more than the pool could earn in entrance fees. In response, a local campaign group collected 4,200 signatures and organized a swim-in on a cold Sunday morning. Since then, the council has agreed to keep the pool open until at least 2028 while it looks for a private operator to take over its management.","q":"What has the council decided since then?","o":["To close the pool in 2028","To hand the pool to schools immediately","To keep it open until at least 2028","To build a new pool in the north"],"a":2,"zh":"市議會已同意泳池至少營運到2028年，同時尋找民間營運者。"}]};
